1
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:11,210
MR. RAMOJI RAO
WILL FOREVER REMAIN IN OUR HEARTS

2
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:25,290
Thank you.

3
00:01:35,210 --> 00:01:37,000
Sir, you got a parcel.

4
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:39,170
- What?
- You got a parcel, sir.

5
00:01:39,790 --> 00:01:42,830
I didn't order anything.
Who sent this?

6
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,960
I don't know, sir.
It just got delivered.

7
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:46,500
Hey, Naveen!

8
00:01:47,380 --> 00:01:50,080
How many times have I told you
not to let strangers in?

9
00:01:50,170 --> 00:01:51,790
Just hand it over to security.

10
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,960
Idiots! Just leave!

11
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:47,380
"Karma has risen.
This is the beginning of the end."

12
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,580
"Hello, David."

13
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:53,000
"Alias Kishore."

14
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:03,790
Someone is trying to unearth a past
that was buried 25 years ago.

15
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:07,000
Who could it be?

16
00:03:24,170 --> 00:03:25,500
Vishnu, 

17
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:27,670
it's been four weeks

18
00:03:28,210 --> 00:03:30,630
since you said you'd be back in four days.

19
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:32,880
Waiting for you is one thing, 

20
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:36,750
but when Shravya keeps asking
when her dad is coming back, 

21
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:40,790
it's hard to keep telling her
you'll come tomorrow.

22
00:03:49,670 --> 00:03:52,710
If you're unhappy with the job, 
you can always come back home.

23
00:03:52,790 --> 00:03:54,880
There's nothing to worry about.

24
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,330
Mom, why isn't this fish moving?

25
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:02,960
Fishy, are you asleep?

26
00:04:03,290 --> 00:04:05,580
It's not asleep. It might be dead.

27
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,290
I've told you so many times
not to overfeed it.

28
00:04:14,290 --> 00:04:16,380
A telegram for Jyothi.

29
00:04:24,250 --> 00:04:26,330
- Sent from?
- Tanuku Sugar Factory.

30
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,460
Who sent it?

31
00:04:28,540 --> 00:04:31,330
Did Dad send it?
Tell me, Mom.

32
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:38,170
Did Dad send that, Mom?

33
00:05:01,210 --> 00:05:03,290
Mom, what happened?

34
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:08,500
Mom, what happened?

35
00:05:24,420 --> 00:05:26,880
Where are we heading now?

36
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:28,960
Are we going to Dad?

37
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:30,750
Mom, tell me.

38
00:05:31,250 --> 00:05:35,250
What if Dad comes home while we're away?

39
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:39,500
Mom!

40
00:06:26,330 --> 00:06:28,420
Mom.

41
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:40,080
Mom.

42
00:06:40,710 --> 00:06:42,500
Wake up, Mom.

43
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:07,580
Why is he calling at this hour?

44
00:07:13,710 --> 00:07:15,330
Tell me.

45
00:07:16,710 --> 00:07:18,790
You're the one who has to answer.

46
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:21,250
Did you find it or not?

47
00:07:21,330 --> 00:07:23,210
- We'll talk tomorrow.
- Hey!

48
00:07:23,290 --> 00:07:26,630
There's nothing more to discuss.
The one week you asked for is over.

49
00:07:26,710 --> 00:07:28,500
Did you forget about this too?

50
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:29,880
I didn't. It's on my mind.

51
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,080
Then you should've called me!

52
00:07:33,250 --> 00:07:35,630
Cut to the chase.
I'm coming to your house now.

53
00:07:35,710 --> 00:07:37,540
Give me my share!

54
00:07:37,630 --> 00:07:40,670
Or else, I'll tell the cops everything.

55
00:07:40,750 --> 00:07:42,830
- Hey!
- I don't care about myself.

56
00:07:43,170 --> 00:07:45,330
I'll drag you out into the street.

57
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:47,500
Don't do it, man.

58
00:07:48,130 --> 00:07:50,210
Hey.

59
00:07:51,330 --> 00:07:53,420
He'll mess everything up if he gets here.

60
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:55,710
He's probably very drunk.

61
00:07:55,830 --> 00:07:58,130
Why would they approve it? Already…

62
00:07:58,580 --> 00:08:00,290
To hell with these two!

63
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:02,500
Why would the bank trust us?

64
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:05,630
Hello, Karthik?

65
00:08:05,830 --> 00:08:07,170
Am I a burden to you…

66
00:08:07,250 --> 00:08:08,460
Hello?

67
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:11,000
Have you forgotten how good I was to you?

68
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:14,630
Who is this?

69
00:08:14,710 --> 00:08:17,130
…might lose the job
for helping you get the loan.

70
00:08:38,289 --> 00:08:39,580
Damn it!

71
00:08:44,790 --> 00:08:47,920
Karthik, stop messing with me.
I know it's you.

72
00:09:59,250 --> 00:10:02,880
Blood Moon bleeds in the sky

73
00:10:04,790 --> 00:10:07,580
As he strides into the night

74
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:09,250
Vinay!

75
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:11,330
Monsters shiver in the dark

76
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:12,880
Vinay!

77
00:10:14,210 --> 00:10:18,880
As he walks towards
The heart of the unknown

78
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:24,040
Out in the rain
He's on his own

79
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:29,210
All through the night
He hunts alone

80
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:34,330
Fire in the lights
Blood on the floor

81
00:10:35,210 --> 00:10:39,960
Nowhere to run
Settle the score

82
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,960
Sirens wail a warning cry

83
00:10:47,250 --> 00:10:50,710
He smells the danger in the air

84
00:10:52,330 --> 00:10:55,710
Behold, the writing's on the wall

85
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:01,420
He tears the web of lies apart

86
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:04,790
The suicide victim is Vinay, sir.
A final-year engineering student.

87
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:06,750
How long have you been in this job, Latha?

88
00:11:06,830 --> 00:11:07,880
It's been six months.

89
00:11:07,960 --> 00:11:11,040
With just six months' experience, 
you can tell

90
00:11:11,130 --> 00:11:13,210
if it was suicide or murder?

91
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:18,500
If he jumped on his own, it's suicide.

92
00:11:19,670 --> 00:11:21,830
If he fell by accident, 
it was an accident.

93
00:11:23,290 --> 00:11:25,290
If someone pushed him…

94
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:27,460
It's murder.

95
00:12:09,710 --> 00:12:11,960
- Get the past two weeks' call records.
- Sir.

96
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,580
The cops just went in.

97
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:48,000
- Srinu.
- Sir.

98
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:50,630
Find the landline number
and give it to the station.

99
00:12:50,710 --> 00:12:52,790
Tell them to contact us in an emergency.

100
00:12:53,170 --> 00:12:54,080
Okay, sir.

101
00:12:54,170 --> 00:12:55,960
Where is Gangadhar?

102
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:58,330
He's coming, sir.
He's out on the balcony.

103
00:13:08,750 --> 00:13:10,920
- So sorry for your loss.
- Please be seated.

104
00:13:13,630 --> 00:13:15,960
The postmortem report
will take some time.

105
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:18,290
If you cooperate with us, 

106
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:21,580
we'll do our best to release
your son's body as soon as possible.

107
00:13:22,130 --> 00:13:23,170
Alright, sir.

108
00:13:23,250 --> 00:13:25,330
What I mean is--

109
00:13:28,790 --> 00:13:31,460
Srinu, clear the area.

110
00:13:32,210 --> 00:13:33,250
Okay, sir.

111
00:13:33,330 --> 00:13:35,000
Everyone, please step outside.

112
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:36,580
Please leave the room.

113
00:13:36,670 --> 00:13:38,750
Please step out.

114
00:13:40,790 --> 00:13:42,210
So tell me.

115
00:13:42,290 --> 00:13:44,380
What exactly happened last night?

116
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:48,330
There's no point talking
about right or wrong now.

117
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:51,080
- Parvathi, how many times do I--
- Hey, stop bickering!

118
00:13:51,170 --> 00:13:53,330
Do you even realize what time it is?

119
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:55,670
You started arguing at 10 p.m.
Now it's 3 a.m.

120
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:03,670
There's no reason for suspicion.

121
00:14:03,750 --> 00:14:07,920
He got a call last night
and went up to the terrace to answer it.

122
00:14:12,580 --> 00:14:14,130
Time?

123
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:18,040
It must have been around 3 a.m.

124
00:14:19,710 --> 00:14:21,790
Why were you still awake at that hour?

125
00:14:25,130 --> 00:14:26,540
Well…

126
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:29,790
I was asleep here in the hall.

127
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:33,790
I woke up when I heard him open the door.

128
00:14:34,130 --> 00:14:38,080
He could've answered the call in his room.
Why did he go up to the terrace?

129
00:14:39,290 --> 00:14:40,960
I don't know.

130
00:14:41,670 --> 00:14:44,920
- How old is Vinay?
- Around 20 or 21?

131
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:47,880
- Is it 20 or 21?
- 21.

132
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:53,580
What do you do, sir?

133
00:14:53,670 --> 00:14:55,920
- What do you mean?
- I mean, what's your job?

134
00:14:57,710 --> 00:15:01,080
My wife works as a head nurse
at a government hospital.

135
00:15:01,750 --> 00:15:03,830
I asked about your job.

136
00:15:06,710 --> 00:15:10,710
I used to own a jewelry store, 
but it was robbed, and I lost everything.

137
00:15:10,790 --> 00:15:12,880
I reported it to the police back then.

138
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:16,130
No one has bothered with it since.

139
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:19,460
So you're not working, 
which means you have no income.

140
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:25,130
Did Vinay have any life insurance?

141
00:15:25,210 --> 00:15:26,710
What?

142
00:15:27,210 --> 00:15:28,880
What are you talking about?

143
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:32,500
Are you saying we killed our son
for the insurance money?

144
00:15:33,670 --> 00:15:37,330
Why have you come here, 
and what are you asking us?

145
00:15:38,830 --> 00:15:41,170
We're already in deep pain
from losing our son.

146
00:15:41,960 --> 00:15:44,420
He didn't sleep last night.
He was drunk too.

147
00:15:44,830 --> 00:15:48,170
And a fight broke out, 
so he definitely won't tell the truth.

148
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:51,880
Was there any fight in the house
last night?

149
00:15:52,630 --> 00:15:54,130
No.

150
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:59,040
Do Vinay's friends come over often?

151
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:03,580
- No.
- Sir, think carefully before answering.

152
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:10,040
His friend Karthik comes over
once in a while.

153
00:16:10,630 --> 00:16:12,710
I'm coming to your house now.

154
00:16:15,330 --> 00:16:17,420
I want to see Vinay's room.

155
00:16:39,210 --> 00:16:40,170
What's this?

156
00:16:40,250 --> 00:16:42,830
Your son made it look locked
from the outside.

157
00:16:43,250 --> 00:16:45,330
That means

158
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:47,960
he's trying to hide something from you.

159
00:16:51,210 --> 00:16:54,080
- Why don't you get a haircut?
- I'll do it later, Mom.

160
00:16:54,630 --> 00:16:56,250
It's for style.

161
00:16:56,330 --> 00:16:58,920
Hey, did you take my bike out last night?

162
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:01,080
Me? No.

163
00:17:01,670 --> 00:17:04,500
Then why is it parked in a different spot?

164
00:17:05,329 --> 00:17:07,329
It happened the night before last, too.

165
00:17:07,420 --> 00:17:09,670
How can you remember that
when you were drunk?

166
00:17:09,750 --> 00:17:11,170
Hey!

167
00:17:11,290 --> 00:17:13,329
Hey. Idiot.

168
00:17:13,420 --> 00:17:15,500
Oh, yes, tell me something.

169
00:17:15,579 --> 00:17:18,920
I came to your room at 3 a.m.
the other day, and you weren't there.

170
00:17:20,710 --> 00:17:24,130
What do you mean?
I might have been in the bathroom.

171
00:17:53,460 --> 00:17:56,170
- These aren't yours, are they?
- No.

172
00:17:59,540 --> 00:18:00,830
Sir.

173
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:05,500
They look like random scribbles.

174
00:18:05,790 --> 00:18:07,210
No.

175
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:10,210
They look like the scribblings
of someone who's suicidal.

176
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:34,080
- Call him.
- Okay, sir.

177
00:18:34,830 --> 00:18:36,920
Sir, please come with me.

178
00:18:40,210 --> 00:18:42,290
Is that Vinay's handwriting?

179
00:18:42,960 --> 00:18:45,040
I'm not sure about it, sir.

180
00:18:47,750 --> 00:18:48,710
Hold on.

181
00:18:48,790 --> 00:18:50,880
- Latha, check who's calling.
- Sir.

182
00:18:54,210 --> 00:18:55,830
- What do you know about your son?
- Hello.

183
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:58,330
He's only 20 and already taking drugs, 
and you don't know.

184
00:18:58,420 --> 00:19:01,790
You don't know his handwriting.
You don't even know his age.

185
00:19:02,830 --> 00:19:04,210
What?!

186
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:07,580
- Okay.
- Sir…

187
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,500
- Sir--
- Wait.

188
00:19:10,460 --> 00:19:11,630
- Sir.
- What?

189
00:19:11,710 --> 00:19:14,330
I need to tell you something.
Can we please step out?

190
00:19:18,210 --> 00:19:21,080
- What's so urgent?
- Sir, it's the postmortem lab.

191
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:23,500
Vinay was murdered. It wasn't suicide.

192
00:19:24,670 --> 00:19:27,420
You asked me not to jump to conclusions.
I remember.

193
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,380
But this is clearly murder, sir.

194
00:19:29,460 --> 00:19:31,670
- There's a bullet in Vinay's skull.
- Bullet?

195
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:36,540
Are you going to say that if he was shot, 
it's murder, 

196
00:19:36,630 --> 00:19:38,960
and if he shot himself, it's suicide?

197
00:19:39,040 --> 00:19:41,080
But there was no gun on the terrace.

198
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:43,540
Could you please hush up?

199
00:19:45,380 --> 00:19:47,460
Bullet in the skull?

200
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,580
How did we miss this, Srinu?

201
00:19:49,670 --> 00:19:50,630
Well…

202
00:19:50,710 --> 00:19:52,790
His parents are hiding something.

203
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:56,580
What if we question the neighbors?

204
00:19:57,330 --> 00:19:59,420
How many apartments are there here?

205
00:20:01,540 --> 00:20:03,540
There are four blocks in this community.

206
00:20:03,630 --> 00:20:05,250
And 32 apartments in this block.

207
00:20:05,330 --> 00:20:06,920
One is available for rent.

208
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,830
Two are locked.

209
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:10,630
That means 29 are occupied.

210
00:20:10,710 --> 00:20:13,000
Let's say there are four people
per apartment.

211
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,540
That makes 116 neighbors.

212
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:18,830
Wouldn't someone among them
have some useful information?

213
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:21,000
Let's find out.

214
00:20:24,420 --> 00:20:27,960
Gangadhar usually spends his time
idling around the house, 

215
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:29,960
smoking and drinking.

216
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:32,130
Parvathi is so kind.

217
00:20:32,790 --> 00:20:36,960
She even gave us money to pay
our children's school tuition a few times.

218
00:20:37,420 --> 00:20:40,250
Parvathi sometimes works night shifts
at the hospital.

219
00:20:40,330 --> 00:20:43,710
And Vinay used to go out
around 10 or 11 p.m.

220
00:20:44,130 --> 00:20:46,210
Parvathi is a very nice person.

221
00:20:46,290 --> 00:20:47,500
But Gangadhar is…

222
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:49,670
Gangadhar borrowed 50, 000 rupees from me.

223
00:20:49,750 --> 00:20:52,580
He gets very rude when I ask him
to pay me back.

224
00:20:52,670 --> 00:20:54,880
I helped Gangadhar get a bank loan.

225
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:57,380
But he never pays his loan installments
on time.

226
00:20:57,460 --> 00:20:58,880
They are a decent family.

227
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,540
We don't know much about them.

228
00:21:00,630 --> 00:21:02,710
- I don't know.
- I don't know.

229
00:21:03,130 --> 00:21:05,880
Did you hear any sounds
from their apartment last night?

230
00:21:05,960 --> 00:21:08,580
- Sounds?
- I mean, like…

231
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:11,040
Like a gunshot?

232
00:21:12,630 --> 00:21:14,790
- A gunshot, right?
- Not exactly.

233
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:16,080
But something similar.

234
00:21:16,170 --> 00:21:19,080
First he asks for 555 cigarettes, 
then he asks for Marlboro.

235
00:21:19,170 --> 00:21:21,040
We don't know much about them.

236
00:21:21,130 --> 00:21:23,580
- We don't know.
- We moved in here recently.

237
00:21:23,790 --> 00:21:25,710
You and Vinay attend the same college.

238
00:21:25,790 --> 00:21:29,000
Same college, 
but we're in different departments, sir.

239
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:31,750
Why are you tense, dear?

240
00:21:31,830 --> 00:21:35,000
I'm not tense.
We're in different departments.

241
00:21:35,540 --> 00:21:37,630
Did Vinay attend college regularly?

242
00:21:38,040 --> 00:21:41,330
How would I know, sir?
We're in different departments.

243
00:21:42,460 --> 00:21:44,420
Do you know any of Vinay's friends?

244
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:46,580
We're in different…

245
00:21:47,500 --> 00:21:50,330
Yeah, you're both
in different departments.

246
00:21:52,460 --> 00:21:55,540
I'm the regional manager
at Kaveri Chit Fund.

247
00:21:55,630 --> 00:21:59,210
Parvathi asked me to recommend
her husband for a job there.

248
00:21:59,290 --> 00:22:02,040
She took the application form
from me yesterday.

249
00:22:03,500 --> 00:22:05,750
The husband and wife
are always fighting.

250
00:22:06,210 --> 00:22:08,290
It was very hard on their son.

251
00:22:09,460 --> 00:22:12,040
Is it my fault if the bank doesn't
approve the loan?

252
00:22:13,710 --> 00:22:16,920
I can't keep up with expenses
like loan payments, college tuition

253
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:17,920
and maintenance.

254
00:22:18,500 --> 00:22:20,920
I've told you many times
that I won't do any job.

255
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:24,580
I had people working under me before.
How can I work under someone now?

256
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:27,540
When you lose the kingdom, 
you lose the throne.

257
00:22:28,290 --> 00:22:30,670
So you admit
that I used to live like a king.

258
00:22:31,080 --> 00:22:32,750
I'll be like this until death.

259
00:22:32,830 --> 00:22:34,920
Until my death?

260
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:46,130
I'm heading to the hospital.

261
00:23:08,040 --> 00:23:12,040
Just because there is darkness
Doesn't mean it owns the place

262
00:23:12,750 --> 00:23:16,750
The full moon never trembles in fear

263
00:23:17,580 --> 00:23:21,580
The stars never abandon the sky

264
00:23:22,460 --> 00:23:26,290
Simply because light seems distant

265
00:23:27,130 --> 00:23:31,130
Even when heavy rains pour down
And the weather turns harsh

266
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:35,960
The raindrops eventually nourish
A tender new leaf

267
00:23:36,750 --> 00:23:40,750
As long as breath remains beside you

268
00:23:41,580 --> 00:23:45,580
Hope for tomorrow will stay with you

269
00:23:46,330 --> 00:23:50,330
How much longer?
How many more years?

270
00:23:51,130 --> 00:23:55,130
Let go of such doubts

271
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:59,960
I have always been here for you

272
00:24:00,710 --> 00:24:04,710
Let that be the message
You carry within yourself

273
00:24:42,670 --> 00:24:46,670
Just because your eyes
Refuse to believe

274
00:24:47,790 --> 00:24:51,790
Can the truth ever change?

275
00:24:52,580 --> 00:24:56,580
The hidden sorrows behind your gaze

276
00:24:57,420 --> 00:25:01,420
Will one day fade away like a dream

277
00:25:02,290 --> 00:25:06,290
The ocean that touches both shores

278
00:25:06,960 --> 00:25:10,960
Never stops to choose a side

279
00:25:11,830 --> 00:25:15,830
The twilight between day and night

280
00:25:16,670 --> 00:25:20,880
Has already told us this story

281
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:23,960
Gangadhar borrowed 300, 000 rupees
from me a year ago.

282
00:25:24,040 --> 00:25:25,880
He hasn't paid me a penny yet.

283
00:25:25,960 --> 00:25:29,080
He keeps making excuses
and hiding from me.

284
00:25:29,170 --> 00:25:30,420
Have some shame.

285
00:25:30,500 --> 00:25:34,630
Life is the meeting point
Of light and darkness

286
00:25:35,290 --> 00:25:39,290
Learning to live with both
Is how we continue our journey

287
00:25:39,880 --> 00:25:43,880
As long as breath remains beside you

288
00:25:44,670 --> 00:25:48,670
Hope for tomorrow will stay with you

289
00:25:49,420 --> 00:25:53,420
How much longer?
How many more years?

290
00:25:54,210 --> 00:25:58,210
Let go of such doubts

291
00:25:59,040 --> 00:26:03,040
I have always been here for you

292
00:26:03,830 --> 00:26:07,830
Let that be the message
You carry within yourself

293
00:26:11,630 --> 00:26:13,960
Mom, where's my ID card? I can't find it.

294
00:26:14,040 --> 00:26:16,130
Mom, where is it?
Time is ticking.

295
00:26:18,830 --> 00:26:20,920
He does this every single day.

296
00:26:23,830 --> 00:26:25,500
You'll find it if you keep your eyes open.

297
00:26:25,580 --> 00:26:27,290
- Okay.
- What's with this new habit?

298
00:26:27,380 --> 00:26:30,580
- You come home late and forget everything.
- Enough, Mom.

299
00:26:32,420 --> 00:26:34,500
Bye, take care.

300
00:26:47,540 --> 00:26:50,250
Hey, we found it in Vinay's room, right?

301
00:26:52,040 --> 00:26:54,130
Sir would be furious if he found out.

302
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:00,210
I have no cigarettes.

303
00:27:00,290 --> 00:27:02,380
Are you going to snitch on me?

304
00:27:07,080 --> 00:27:08,960
Sir.

305
00:27:09,040 --> 00:27:10,420
Idiot.

306
00:27:11,210 --> 00:27:13,500
Sorry, sir.
I'll put this in the evidence bag.

307
00:27:14,250 --> 00:27:16,250
Do we have Vinay's call records?

308
00:27:16,330 --> 00:27:17,920
I'll look into it, sir.

309
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:19,630
There's a lawyer on the second floor.

310
00:27:19,710 --> 00:27:22,250
See if he has a fax machine
and tell them to send it there.

311
00:27:22,330 --> 00:27:23,830
Okay, sir.

312
00:27:30,580 --> 00:27:32,670
Sir, shall I bring you some tea?

313
00:27:46,540 --> 00:27:48,330
Sir, did you notice something?

314
00:27:48,420 --> 00:27:50,630
The things in this house
are quite eclectic.

315
00:27:57,460 --> 00:28:01,670
The lady detective
Quite effective

316
00:28:03,380 --> 00:28:05,460
Did you see that sticker on the chest?

317
00:28:07,710 --> 00:28:10,080
The same sticker is in a couple
of other places.

318
00:28:10,170 --> 00:28:14,170
I think Gangadhar might have run
an antiques business

319
00:28:14,250 --> 00:28:16,460
before opening his jewelry shop.

320
00:28:16,830 --> 00:28:20,460
After closing it down, he seems to have
kept some of those items at home.

321
00:28:23,500 --> 00:28:26,830
Sir, no one around here seems to know
anyone in this apartment.

322
00:28:26,920 --> 00:28:28,540
Certainly not anyone in this apartment.

323
00:28:28,630 --> 00:28:31,790
No one saw anyone arguing on the terrace
last night.

324
00:28:32,750 --> 00:28:35,670
These are Vinay's call records.
This is quite serious, sir.

325
00:28:36,250 --> 00:28:39,960
Vinay has been frequently calling
and receiving calls from just one number.

326
00:28:40,040 --> 00:28:41,420
And it's not a personal number.

327
00:28:41,500 --> 00:28:44,170
It's a public coin-operated phone
in Yousufguda.

328
00:28:44,250 --> 00:28:48,210
He got a call from that number
last night at 2:55 a.m.

329
00:28:49,170 --> 00:28:50,790
The call lasted 50 seconds.

330
00:28:50,880 --> 00:28:54,420
He immediately received another call
from an unknown cell phone number.

331
00:28:54,830 --> 00:28:56,920
That call lasted just three seconds.

332
00:28:57,500 --> 00:28:59,580
But Vinay called back immediately.

333
00:29:00,500 --> 00:29:02,580
Did you find out whose number it is?

334
00:29:03,330 --> 00:29:05,420
It belongs to Mercury.

335
00:29:06,040 --> 00:29:08,130
Mercury?

336
00:29:14,250 --> 00:29:15,250
Who's that, sir?

337
00:29:15,330 --> 00:29:17,420
It's Stephen Mercury.

338
00:29:20,250 --> 00:29:22,330
A criminal and a smuggler.

339
00:29:26,750 --> 00:29:30,040
He's already facing charges
for several robberies and ten murders.

340
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:54,920
What connection could a criminal like him
have with a college student?

341
00:29:55,330 --> 00:29:57,630
Why would he call at that hour?

342
00:29:57,710 --> 00:30:00,540
This case is bigger
than it first seemed, sir.

343
00:30:01,750 --> 00:30:04,670
Looks like Vinay did a lot of shady things
before he died.

344
00:30:11,210 --> 00:30:12,670
Hello.

345
00:30:12,750 --> 00:30:13,880
Kishore.

346
00:30:13,960 --> 00:30:16,250
You need my help
with your new case, right?

347
00:30:16,330 --> 00:30:18,420
Do you know where I am?

348
00:30:19,290 --> 00:30:21,380
You'll find me.

349
00:30:21,710 --> 00:30:23,790
Fine. Bring the case file with you.

350
00:30:34,920 --> 00:30:36,710
- Srinu.
- Yes, sir.

351
00:30:36,790 --> 00:30:38,880
Help me move this chest.

352
00:30:48,750 --> 00:30:50,830
There's blood.

353
00:30:52,710 --> 00:30:54,460
I don't know how it got there, sir.

354
00:30:54,540 --> 00:30:56,710
We'll find out soon enough.

355
00:30:56,790 --> 00:30:58,880
Srinu, find out how long it's been there, 

356
00:30:58,960 --> 00:31:02,630
and see if it matches Vinay, 
Gangadhar, or Parvathi.

357
00:31:02,710 --> 00:31:04,790
- Okay, sir.
- Quick.

358
00:31:09,380 --> 00:31:12,250
What is it this time?
Murder, suicide, or an accident?

359
00:31:15,880 --> 00:31:18,040
We couldn't figure it out, 
so I came to you.

360
00:31:26,080 --> 00:31:28,460
Who the heck made you
a sub-inspector, Kishore?

361
00:31:28,540 --> 00:31:32,290
You can't solve a case on your own.
You come running to me for everything.

362
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:34,960
This time, I've got a big one for you.

363
00:31:35,040 --> 00:31:37,540
But I'm busy right now.
I'll look into it later.

364
00:31:43,830 --> 00:31:46,080
Three thousand rupees, sir.

365
00:31:46,170 --> 00:31:48,540
You can buy a job with a bribe, 
but not brains.

366
00:31:50,750 --> 00:31:52,290
It looks like an accident, sir.

367
00:31:52,380 --> 00:31:55,250
But we can't tell if it was really
an accident or murder.

368
00:31:58,790 --> 00:32:02,040
The deceased was Jyothi.
Her husband died in a fire.

369
00:32:02,420 --> 00:32:06,040
She was on her way to collect his body
when this happened.

370
00:32:06,380 --> 00:32:08,460
That's all we know for now, sir.

371
00:32:09,040 --> 00:32:11,380
I called her husband's factory
and confirmed

372
00:32:11,460 --> 00:32:13,210
that the fire really happened.

373
00:32:13,290 --> 00:32:16,290
The evidence was gone
before our team got there.

374
00:32:16,830 --> 00:32:20,000
All we found was the body, a bag, 
and a little girl.

375
00:32:20,630 --> 00:32:22,710
The girl may be 5 years old.

376
00:32:31,250 --> 00:32:36,250
We may have to close this case
as a hit-and-run or leave it unsolved.

377
00:32:40,790 --> 00:32:42,920
But before that, see if you can crack it.

378
00:32:47,330 --> 00:32:49,420
Marley Spirit.

379
00:32:52,920 --> 00:32:54,130
Sir?

380
00:32:54,210 --> 00:32:56,580
Marley Spirit. The car that hit her.

381
00:32:57,920 --> 00:33:00,540
It's a very old and rare model.
A vintage piece.

382
00:33:02,670 --> 00:33:05,250
You can hardly find ten in the city.

383
00:33:05,330 --> 00:33:07,420
How do you know that?

384
00:33:08,210 --> 00:33:10,290
I didn't buy my way into this job.

385
00:33:11,670 --> 00:33:14,580
It shouldn't be that hard
to find that car among the ten.

386
00:33:20,630 --> 00:33:22,710
Marley Spirit.

387
00:33:28,710 --> 00:33:30,790
Let me see that group photo.

388
00:33:33,580 --> 00:33:35,670
We found it in her house, sir.

389
00:33:39,880 --> 00:33:41,170
What is it, sir?

390
00:33:41,250 --> 00:33:43,460
Did you go to the hospital
to find out about Jyothi?

391
00:33:43,540 --> 00:33:44,790
Yes, I did.

392
00:33:44,880 --> 00:33:46,420
Whom did you ask?

393
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:55,130
Your name?

394
00:33:55,210 --> 00:33:56,920
Parvathi.

395
00:33:57,000 --> 00:33:58,960
How long has Jyothi been working here?

396
00:33:59,040 --> 00:34:01,500
Approximately a year.

397
00:34:02,540 --> 00:34:05,130
Did Jyothi ever talk about her past
with you?

398
00:34:08,670 --> 00:34:10,040
They had a love marriage.

399
00:34:10,130 --> 00:34:12,880
Their parents didn't approve, 
so they eloped.

400
00:34:14,210 --> 00:34:16,290
She died in an accident a week ago.

401
00:34:18,540 --> 00:34:21,000
When did Jyothi tell you
that she quit the job?

402
00:34:21,790 --> 00:34:24,830
Today's my last day.
I won't be coming in after today.

403
00:34:25,670 --> 00:34:27,750
- Did your husband get a job?
- Yes.

404
00:34:28,500 --> 00:34:30,710
Oh, congrats! Where?

405
00:34:31,460 --> 00:34:34,080
He's a production manager
at Tanuku Sugar Factory.

406
00:34:34,170 --> 00:34:36,250
He just joined yesterday.

407
00:34:36,630 --> 00:34:39,920
He said he'd come next week
and take Shravya and me with him.

408
00:34:40,630 --> 00:34:44,130
So, you don't have to work
to support your small family.

409
00:34:46,080 --> 00:34:47,830
What else?

410
00:34:48,420 --> 00:34:51,000
My dream is to become a writer.

411
00:34:51,710 --> 00:34:54,250
From now on, I have to focus on it.

412
00:34:56,040 --> 00:34:59,630
You remind me of the person I once was.

413
00:35:01,170 --> 00:35:03,250
I used to be like you.

414
00:35:03,830 --> 00:35:06,710
But I spent my life supporting
my husband's dreams

415
00:35:06,790 --> 00:35:08,880
and providing for our family.

416
00:35:09,630 --> 00:35:13,630
Now, I've forgotten
that I have a life of my own.

417
00:35:15,830 --> 00:35:18,670
At least you have your life back.

418
00:35:31,250 --> 00:35:33,330
Give this to Shravya.

419
00:35:34,670 --> 00:35:36,750
- All the best.
- Thank you.

420
00:35:41,580 --> 00:35:43,920
I thought she went to Tanuku.

421
00:35:45,670 --> 00:35:49,750
I didn't know she had died
until you told me.

422
00:35:52,000 --> 00:35:54,420
Where's Shravya now?

423
00:35:55,330 --> 00:35:56,790
Poor child.

424
00:35:56,880 --> 00:35:58,960
We sent her to Jyothi's parents.

425
00:36:02,460 --> 00:36:05,290
Do you think there's any link
between these two cases?

426
00:36:37,630 --> 00:36:39,710
Just give me ten days.

427
00:36:40,380 --> 00:36:43,790
I'll do whatever job
you ask me to, Parvathi.

428
00:36:43,880 --> 00:36:47,330
I can't bear the thought
that I made a mistake.

429
00:36:49,130 --> 00:36:51,210
If I'd been a responsible adult…

430
00:36:52,460 --> 00:36:54,540
this might not have happened last night.

431
00:36:57,710 --> 00:36:59,790
And Vinay might still be with us.

432
00:37:03,290 --> 00:37:05,380
Forgive me, Parvathi.

433
00:37:06,540 --> 00:37:08,630
Please, Parvathi.

434
00:37:09,080 --> 00:37:11,170
Please say something, Parvathi.

435
00:37:13,960 --> 00:37:17,080
Why do you need to change
after you've lost everything?

436
00:37:18,580 --> 00:37:22,170
Even if we change now, 
it won't bring Vinay back, right?

437
00:37:32,380 --> 00:37:33,670
Parvathi.

438
00:37:36,750 --> 00:37:39,290
What happened last night was an accident.

439
00:37:40,330 --> 00:37:43,580
I didn't even know
there was a bullet in that gun.

440
00:37:47,710 --> 00:37:50,630
I know you weren't aware
there was a bullet in the gun.

441
00:37:51,670 --> 00:37:53,750
Let's not discuss these things now.

442
00:37:55,330 --> 00:37:57,420
You believe me, right?

443
00:38:01,290 --> 00:38:03,380
Ma'am, sir is asking for you.

444
00:38:05,380 --> 00:38:08,130
If a 20-year-old boy commits suicide, 

445
00:38:08,210 --> 00:38:10,290
he's either a coward

446
00:38:10,880 --> 00:38:13,460
or there must be
a strong reason behind it.

447
00:38:14,630 --> 00:38:18,290
If it's neither of those, there must
have been a fight at home last night.

448
00:38:19,790 --> 00:38:21,580
Do you even realize what time it is?

449
00:38:21,880 --> 00:38:24,170
You started arguing at 10 p.m.
Now it's 3 a.m.

450
00:38:24,250 --> 00:38:26,630
You two are always fighting, 
day and night.

451
00:38:27,250 --> 00:38:30,540
You two never agree on anything.
You're making my life miserable!

452
00:38:31,790 --> 00:38:33,380
If you can't live together, get a divorce.

453
00:38:33,460 --> 00:38:34,830
Hey!

454
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:41,460
I'll kill you if you say another word
beyond your years.

455
00:38:41,790 --> 00:38:45,420
Ma'am, if a 20-year-old boy
commits suicide…

456
00:38:45,710 --> 00:38:47,830
He's asking what happened last night.

457
00:38:50,420 --> 00:38:52,500
Sir, I already said--

458
00:38:53,460 --> 00:38:55,040
- Srinu.
- Sir.

459
00:38:55,130 --> 00:38:57,210
Take him away.

460
00:39:05,040 --> 00:39:08,500
How can you be so sure
my son committed suicide?

461
00:39:08,580 --> 00:39:11,540
Fine, I won't call it suicide.
Let's put that aside for now.

462
00:39:11,630 --> 00:39:15,290
Could you please briefly explain
everything that happened yesterday?

463
00:39:16,290 --> 00:39:19,460
I wasn't at home, sir.
I went to the hospital.

464
00:39:20,380 --> 00:39:22,920
She isn't lying, 
but she's trying to hide the truth.

465
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:24,580
What could it be?

466
00:39:24,670 --> 00:39:26,290
Latha.

467
00:39:26,380 --> 00:39:27,630
Sir.

468
00:39:27,710 --> 00:39:30,710
This college letter says
Vinay hasn't been attending classes.

469
00:39:32,080 --> 00:39:34,130
We found this in your bedroom.

470
00:39:34,210 --> 00:39:38,130
Usually, parents get very angry
when they receive a letter like this.

471
00:39:38,630 --> 00:39:40,710
How did you react when you saw this?

472
00:39:43,290 --> 00:39:47,460
Look, I'm not trying to make you upset.

473
00:39:48,670 --> 00:39:51,330
Whatever I ask, my intention is the same.

474
00:39:51,880 --> 00:39:53,960
To find out what caused Vinay's death.

475
00:39:54,670 --> 00:39:56,750
So, please cooperate.

476
00:40:00,040 --> 00:40:02,670
That day, I went to Vinay's college.

477
00:40:24,880 --> 00:40:27,130
Not him.
I should give you an earful first.

478
00:40:27,830 --> 00:40:30,710
How many times have I told you
not to smoke in the house?

479
00:40:32,080 --> 00:40:34,830
You should be ashamed of deceiving me.

480
00:40:35,420 --> 00:40:38,710
Do you know how hard I work
to pay your college fees?

481
00:40:39,080 --> 00:40:41,960
You leave home with a bag
as if you're going to college, 

482
00:40:42,040 --> 00:40:43,210
but you don't.

483
00:40:43,630 --> 00:40:45,170
Then what do you do all day?

484
00:40:45,250 --> 00:40:46,580
Mom…

485
00:40:46,670 --> 00:40:48,580
I go to college every day.

486
00:40:48,670 --> 00:40:50,420
I just didn't go today.

487
00:40:50,500 --> 00:40:52,580
I'll smack you if you lie to me.

488
00:40:55,210 --> 00:40:56,830
When did you start smoking?

489
00:40:56,920 --> 00:41:00,710
Smoking? I suspected it when I found
two cigarettes missing from my pack.

490
00:41:01,750 --> 00:41:03,250
Turn off the damn TV!

491
00:41:03,330 --> 00:41:06,250
Why are you shouting at me
as if I did something wrong?

492
00:41:06,460 --> 00:41:08,380
Hey, why aren't you going to college?

493
00:41:08,460 --> 00:41:10,380
Zip it, Dad.

494
00:41:10,460 --> 00:41:12,420
Don't interfere.

495
00:41:12,500 --> 00:41:15,130
Get your own act together
before you lecture me.

496
00:41:15,210 --> 00:41:16,080
Hey.

497
00:41:16,170 --> 00:41:18,790
How many times do I have to say
I'm going to college?

498
00:41:19,380 --> 00:41:20,750
So annoying.

499
00:41:30,790 --> 00:41:32,880
Then what's this?

500
00:41:37,420 --> 00:41:41,290
Have you noticed any unusual behavior
in Vinay recently?

501
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:45,540
He often forgot where he put things.

502
00:41:46,420 --> 00:41:51,330
He'd raise a ruckus every day, 
saying his things were missing.

503
00:41:57,420 --> 00:41:58,540
One day…

504
00:41:58,630 --> 00:42:01,880
- Where to? Eat your dinner.
- Going to a movie. I'll eat outside.

505
00:42:01,960 --> 00:42:04,000
What should I do with this rice?

506
00:42:04,130 --> 00:42:05,460
Make it into tamarind rice.

507
00:42:05,540 --> 00:42:07,630
Did you take your keys?

508
00:42:10,210 --> 00:42:12,290
He remembers this well.

509
00:42:13,920 --> 00:42:16,000
And the next day…

510
00:42:19,080 --> 00:42:21,170
What did you lose this time?

511
00:42:21,710 --> 00:42:23,420
I'm talking to you.

512
00:42:23,500 --> 00:42:26,210
I'll search for it too, 
if you tell me what it is.

513
00:42:29,580 --> 00:42:32,960
You even forgot what you're looking for?
Where did you put it?

514
00:42:33,040 --> 00:42:35,250
If I knew, I'd look there myself.

515
00:42:38,000 --> 00:42:41,080
This house and the people in it

516
00:42:41,170 --> 00:42:43,250
are irredeemable!

517
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:46,630
What's in it?
That's typical of Vinay, right?

518
00:42:47,130 --> 00:42:48,630
No.

519
00:42:48,710 --> 00:42:53,630
After that, he started seriously searching
the whole house for something.

520
00:42:54,290 --> 00:42:57,210
And he even looked somewhat disturbed.

521
00:42:57,880 --> 00:43:00,880
He searched his room
in an agitated state yesterday too.

522
00:43:01,330 --> 00:43:03,420
But you said you weren't home yesterday.

523
00:43:06,580 --> 00:43:09,130
I was on the afternoon shift yesterday.

524
00:43:10,750 --> 00:43:13,000
I left for work after 2 p.m.

525
00:43:15,960 --> 00:43:18,420
I have no reason to lie to you.

526
00:43:25,540 --> 00:43:27,830
Did Vinay and Gangadhar ever quarrel?

527
00:43:28,710 --> 00:43:30,790
I can see

528
00:43:31,130 --> 00:43:34,670
that you're asking these questions
based on what the neighbors told you.

529
00:43:36,130 --> 00:43:39,500
Everyone sees things
from their own perspective.

530
00:43:39,580 --> 00:43:41,670
But why not look at it differently?

531
00:43:43,130 --> 00:43:45,330
What could they have said about Vinay?

532
00:43:45,420 --> 00:43:48,920
That he skipped college
and loafed around with his friends?

533
00:43:50,210 --> 00:43:52,290
That's all, isn't it?

534
00:43:52,670 --> 00:43:55,670
They saw one side of Vinay.
At home, he was different.

535
00:43:57,500 --> 00:43:59,580
He was a responsible son.

536
00:44:29,080 --> 00:44:31,170
What's Dad's problem, Mom?

537
00:44:32,920 --> 00:44:35,540
The problem lies with all of us, 
not just him.

538
00:44:36,670 --> 00:44:39,250
Maybe you're right, 
but Dad is the solution.

539
00:44:40,040 --> 00:44:42,750
If there's a problem, 
there'll be a solution.

540
00:44:43,290 --> 00:44:46,580
So we must have one too, right?

541
00:44:49,670 --> 00:44:51,460
How much do you need?

542
00:44:52,460 --> 00:44:54,540
He was eager to help.

543
00:44:54,960 --> 00:44:58,420
Mom, just tell me. How much do we need
to solve all our problems?

544
00:45:00,330 --> 00:45:02,920
- Can you get me whatever I ask for?
- Just say it.

545
00:45:06,170 --> 00:45:09,420
The respect we lost
in front of the neighbors.

546
00:45:10,630 --> 00:45:13,830
The faith your dad lost in life.

547
00:45:15,500 --> 00:45:18,420
The sleepless nights I spent
working night shifts.

548
00:45:19,880 --> 00:45:22,250
The quality education you're missing.

549
00:45:23,920 --> 00:45:26,000
Can you bring all that back?

550
00:45:27,330 --> 00:45:29,460
This isn't just about money, son.

551
00:45:30,580 --> 00:45:32,540
It's about change.

552
00:45:32,630 --> 00:45:35,500
We can't force it, and we can't stop it.

553
00:45:36,710 --> 00:45:38,630
It takes time.

554
00:45:38,710 --> 00:45:43,880
It takes time for people to change
and problems to be solved.

555
00:45:45,500 --> 00:45:48,670
You kids think
money can change everything.

556
00:45:49,710 --> 00:45:54,380
But we believe money will come
when everything changes for the better.

557
00:46:00,670 --> 00:46:02,750
What's your ambition in life?

558
00:46:05,880 --> 00:46:07,920
Do you know what my ambition is?

559
00:46:08,000 --> 00:46:11,380
Have you ever thought about finding out

560
00:46:12,500 --> 00:46:14,580
what your mom wants?

561
00:46:16,460 --> 00:46:18,540
Tell me now.

562
00:46:19,750 --> 00:46:21,830
It's nothing much.

563
00:46:22,670 --> 00:46:24,750
Just a small wish.

564
00:46:25,960 --> 00:46:29,500
At least once, I want all three of us
to sit at this table

565
00:46:30,080 --> 00:46:32,540
and happily eat a meal together.

566
00:46:33,500 --> 00:46:35,580
That's it.

567
00:46:36,960 --> 00:46:38,750
Yes.

568
00:46:38,830 --> 00:46:40,920
Nothing more.

569
00:46:45,420 --> 00:46:48,250
You asked what Dad's problem is, right?

570
00:46:49,290 --> 00:46:53,830
Remember, everyone goes
through a bad phase in life.

571
00:46:54,670 --> 00:46:56,750
Everyone has their downfall.

572
00:46:57,080 --> 00:47:01,330
We should never judge people
based on what they go through.

573
00:47:18,830 --> 00:47:21,080
I think she's telling the truth, sir.

574
00:47:22,170 --> 00:47:24,540
But we're not getting
the information we need.

575
00:47:24,630 --> 00:47:26,330
Two teas, please.

576
00:47:26,420 --> 00:47:29,000
Maybe we're not asking
the right questions.

577
00:47:33,130 --> 00:47:35,380
Why don't we ask her
about the bullet, sir?

578
00:47:45,750 --> 00:47:48,040
If they're involved, they won't tell us.

579
00:47:48,880 --> 00:47:52,500
If they're not, it'll shatter them.

580
00:47:53,250 --> 00:47:55,460
Then we can't do much.

581
00:47:55,540 --> 00:47:57,630
We'll be helpless either way.

582
00:47:58,460 --> 00:48:00,420
Did we get the forensic report, Srinu?

583
00:48:00,500 --> 00:48:03,040
The report isn't ready yet, 
but I spoke to them.

584
00:48:03,130 --> 00:48:05,500
They said those bloodstains
were a week old.

585
00:48:05,880 --> 00:48:09,000
And they didn't match
Vinay, Parvathi, or Gangadhar.

586
00:48:09,420 --> 00:48:11,630
So there was a fourth person.

587
00:48:11,710 --> 00:48:14,500
- Could it be Mercury?
- It could be Karthik too.

588
00:48:15,130 --> 00:48:16,830
Did you find out where Karthik is?

589
00:48:16,920 --> 00:48:19,040
Not yet, sir.
Our men are looking for him.

590
00:48:19,130 --> 00:48:22,130
- Why is it taking so long?
- I'll look into it, sir.

591
00:48:23,210 --> 00:48:25,330
- Latha, bring the watchman.
- Sir.

592
00:48:33,790 --> 00:48:34,830
Hello, sir.

593
00:48:34,920 --> 00:48:36,710
- What's your name?
- Venkat Rao, sir.

594
00:48:36,790 --> 00:48:38,920
Mr. Venkat Rao.

595
00:48:39,000 --> 00:48:41,130
Tell me honestly. What was Vinay like?

596
00:48:41,210 --> 00:48:43,170
He was a really good guy.

597
00:48:43,250 --> 00:48:44,920
- Are you from Godavari?
- Yes.

598
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:46,420
Where in Godavari?

599
00:48:46,500 --> 00:48:48,710
- Penugonda, in West Godavari.
- I see.

600
00:48:49,710 --> 00:48:52,630
How are you so sure
that Vinay was a good guy?

601
00:48:52,710 --> 00:48:56,290
Well, he used to tip me
ten or twenty rupees sometimes.

602
00:48:56,380 --> 00:48:59,250
- What? Does tipping make someone good?
- Yes.

603
00:48:59,330 --> 00:49:03,380
If he tipped you, he must've been doing
something shady at home.

604
00:49:03,460 --> 00:49:05,750
- And you were helping him.
- Oh, no!

605
00:49:05,830 --> 00:49:07,920
It was nothing like that.

606
00:49:08,500 --> 00:49:11,670
Sir knows what you and Vinay were up to.

607
00:49:13,080 --> 00:49:16,250
Okay. Vinay had a friend called Karthik.

608
00:49:16,330 --> 00:49:18,250
What do you know about him?

609
00:49:18,330 --> 00:49:19,750
I don't know his name, sir.

610
00:49:19,830 --> 00:49:22,290
But a guy used to come here often.

611
00:49:22,880 --> 00:49:26,210
The other day, Vinay came here
with his friend at 11 p.m.

612
00:49:32,960 --> 00:49:35,750
His friend left in a hurry after 1 a.m.

613
00:49:37,540 --> 00:49:39,920
His hand was bandaged.

614
00:49:40,040 --> 00:49:42,630
I think they must've had a big fight
that night.

615
00:49:42,880 --> 00:49:45,000
Why didn't you tell us this earlier?

616
00:50:11,830 --> 00:50:13,920
The last piece of the puzzle.

617
00:50:42,580 --> 00:50:46,130
Sir, when will you give us Vinay's body?

618
00:50:48,000 --> 00:50:50,080
First, tell me what happened last night.

619
00:50:51,880 --> 00:50:55,580
What else do we need to say?
Aren't you going to let us grieve for him?

620
00:50:56,750 --> 00:50:59,040
We have so many last rites to perform.

621
00:50:59,130 --> 00:51:01,630
I don't understand
what you're still looking for.

622
00:51:01,710 --> 00:51:04,380
You yourself said Vinay committed suicide.

623
00:51:07,330 --> 00:51:10,130
The postmortem report is in.
It wasn't suicide.

624
00:51:13,710 --> 00:51:15,790
It's murder!

625
00:51:18,630 --> 00:51:20,710
Someone shot and killed Vinay.

626
00:51:21,250 --> 00:51:23,250
What are you saying, sir?

627
00:51:23,330 --> 00:51:24,290
Sir.

628
00:51:24,380 --> 00:51:25,670
What…

629
00:51:25,750 --> 00:51:27,830
What do you mean he was shot dead?

630
00:51:28,750 --> 00:51:30,830
The postmortem report.

631
00:51:32,040 --> 00:51:34,130
Sir, who did that?

632
00:51:34,540 --> 00:51:35,460
I'll tell you.

633
00:51:35,540 --> 00:51:37,380
But first, 

634
00:51:37,460 --> 00:51:39,750
I found these torn papers in your dustbin.

635
00:51:40,380 --> 00:51:44,210
It's a job application for the manager
position at Kaveri Chit Fund.

636
00:51:46,540 --> 00:51:49,330
The date shows it was filled out
yesterday.

637
00:51:50,500 --> 00:51:52,210
How did this application get torn?

638
00:51:52,290 --> 00:51:55,630
What's this?
Why are you asking irrelevant questions?

639
00:51:57,920 --> 00:52:00,330
If you tell me yourself, 
it'll be the truth.

640
00:52:00,420 --> 00:52:04,130
If I find out myself, 
you'll be considered guilty.

641
00:52:11,580 --> 00:52:12,580
Last night…

642
00:52:12,670 --> 00:52:14,540
Why are you stuck on something
that won't work?

643
00:52:14,630 --> 00:52:16,250
Parvathi, why do you keep nagging me--

644
00:52:16,330 --> 00:52:17,830
Hey, knock it off!

645
00:52:17,920 --> 00:52:20,040
If you can't live together, get a divorce.

646
00:52:34,880 --> 00:52:38,380
As you said, Vinay went to the terrace
to answer that call.

647
00:52:39,540 --> 00:52:41,630
Please listen to me patiently.

648
00:52:42,830 --> 00:52:47,080
If you go into business, you might make
40, 000 rupees a month at most.

649
00:52:49,130 --> 00:52:51,210
And a job may get you only 10, 000 rupees.

650
00:52:51,830 --> 00:52:53,330
I know it's very little.

651
00:52:53,420 --> 00:52:57,170
But instead of sitting idle, 
that's better, isn't it?

652
00:53:00,130 --> 00:53:02,210
I've filled out the form.

653
00:53:02,670 --> 00:53:05,000
I spoke to the people at the company.

654
00:53:06,040 --> 00:53:08,540
All that's needed is your signature.

655
00:53:24,580 --> 00:53:26,630
You are a working woman.

656
00:53:26,710 --> 00:53:30,920
As far as I know, 
this household depends on your salary.

657
00:53:32,830 --> 00:53:34,920
What he did must have hurt you badly.

658
00:53:36,290 --> 00:53:38,380
You must have been furious.

659
00:53:39,080 --> 00:53:41,250
You really need to be ashamed of yourself.

660
00:53:41,330 --> 00:53:44,710
We have so many problems, 
but you don't even care!

661
00:53:45,040 --> 00:53:47,130
Are you even human?

662
00:53:49,960 --> 00:53:52,210
You don't understand when I speak calmly.

663
00:53:59,670 --> 00:54:02,000
You can't even take it
when she scolds you.

664
00:54:02,080 --> 00:54:04,170
Would you just take it if she hit you?

665
00:54:05,130 --> 00:54:07,210
You must have gone berserk.

666
00:54:14,330 --> 00:54:17,460
Take your anger out on the problems, 
not on people or things.

667
00:54:17,540 --> 00:54:19,630
At least that would serve a purpose.

668
00:54:21,880 --> 00:54:23,960
You want it to serve a purpose?

669
00:54:27,750 --> 00:54:29,830
A purpose?

670
00:54:35,210 --> 00:54:38,000
Now watch. This will serve a purpose.

671
00:54:38,080 --> 00:54:40,170
What the hell are you doing?

672
00:55:11,460 --> 00:55:13,540
The bullet we found in Vinay's head.

673
00:55:17,210 --> 00:55:19,460
It was fired from an antique gun.

674
00:55:21,460 --> 00:55:24,130
And that gun is in your house.
Where is it?

675
00:55:26,790 --> 00:55:28,880
Shall I tell you?

676
00:55:58,210 --> 00:56:00,290
Vinay could have survived the fall.

677
00:56:00,920 --> 00:56:03,880
But the bullet you fired, 

678
00:56:03,960 --> 00:56:06,040
killed him midair.

679
00:56:37,830 --> 00:56:41,130
I didn't expect us to solve this case
so quickly, sir.

680
00:56:42,880 --> 00:56:45,040
Who said this case was closed?

681
00:56:45,130 --> 00:56:46,460
Why do you say that, sir?

682
00:56:46,540 --> 00:56:49,420
We found out who shot Vinay
and arrested Gangadhar.

683
00:56:49,500 --> 00:56:50,830
It's over, isn't it?

684
00:56:50,920 --> 00:56:54,880
We found out who shot Vinay, 
but there's still a lot more to uncover.

685
00:56:56,790 --> 00:56:59,080
What did Vinay and Karthik do at night?

686
00:57:00,630 --> 00:57:05,960
The watchman said Karthik left
late at night with bruises. Why?

687
00:57:07,710 --> 00:57:09,960
Was it Karthik's blood on the mat?

688
00:57:12,460 --> 00:57:13,580
Two weeks ago…

689
00:57:15,000 --> 00:57:18,710
Vinay put something important somewhere
and forgot where he'd put it.

690
00:57:18,790 --> 00:57:21,000
He'd been looking all over the house
for it.

691
00:57:21,130 --> 00:57:22,130
What was it?

692
00:57:24,130 --> 00:57:27,580
What's the connection
between the most-wanted criminal Mercury

693
00:57:28,040 --> 00:57:30,130
and Vinay?

694
00:57:39,330 --> 00:57:41,290
And the important question is…

695
00:57:41,380 --> 00:57:44,790
The bullet hit Vinay by coincidence
when he fell from the building.

696
00:57:46,790 --> 00:57:50,130
Did he fall from the terrace, 
or was he pushed?

697
00:57:54,500 --> 00:57:58,710
And is there anyone else
we need to know about in this case?

698
00:58:10,210 --> 00:58:11,540
"Part 2 coming soon."

699
00:58:34,670 --> 00:58:38,710
I want the contact number for Vinay, 
the author of Newton's Third Law.

700
00:58:39,960 --> 00:58:42,040
Find out.

701
00:59:19,630 --> 00:59:21,710
Hello? Who's this?

702
00:59:25,380 --> 00:59:28,920
Hi, is this Vinay, 
the author of Newton's Third Law?

703
00:59:29,000 --> 00:59:30,500
Yes, speaking.

704
00:59:30,580 --> 00:59:31,750
I'm David.

705
00:59:31,830 --> 00:59:33,920
Is this the right time to talk to you?

706
00:59:34,580 --> 00:59:36,790
Fine, tell me.

707
00:59:36,880 --> 00:59:39,830
First of all, 
congratulations on the huge success.

708
00:59:40,170 --> 00:59:41,580
I just finished your book.

709
00:59:41,670 --> 00:59:43,750
- That was fantastic.
- Thank you.

710
00:59:44,330 --> 00:59:47,250
And I have an interesting

711
00:59:47,750 --> 00:59:49,710
business proposal for you.

712
00:59:49,790 --> 00:59:52,790
Sorry, sir.
But I'm not at all interested in business.

713
00:59:53,330 --> 00:59:55,710
If you don't mind, 
could we meet in person?

714
00:59:56,000 --> 00:59:58,920
Just a half-hour meeting
over a cup of coffee or something.

715
00:59:59,000 --> 01:00:00,710
It isn't like a money-making deal.

716
01:00:00,790 --> 01:00:04,500
It's like an NGO kind of thing
for orphans and poor kids.

717
01:00:05,080 --> 01:00:06,080
If you want, 

718
01:00:06,170 --> 01:00:08,710
I can send my profile to you.
You can take a look.

719
01:00:15,040 --> 01:00:16,040
Please.

720
01:00:16,130 --> 01:00:17,790
Just one meeting.

721
01:00:17,880 --> 01:00:19,630
Jeez, that's fine, sir.

722
01:00:19,710 --> 01:00:21,960
You don't have to plead.

723
01:00:22,960 --> 01:00:24,920
- I'll meet.
- Thank you.

724
01:00:25,000 --> 01:00:27,500
Thank you very much.
I'll take care of your flight tickets.

725
01:00:27,580 --> 01:00:31,330
By the way, are you done with the draft
of the second part?

726
01:00:31,790 --> 01:00:33,790
Yeah. Almost done.

727
01:00:33,880 --> 01:00:36,500
But I'm still working on a better climax.

728
01:00:36,580 --> 01:00:37,580
One more thing.

729
01:00:37,670 --> 01:00:39,750
Why did you name it Newton's Third Law?

730
01:00:40,420 --> 01:00:43,000
I mean, I didn't find any justification.

731
01:00:43,670 --> 01:00:46,500
Sir, Newton's Third Law is nothing but

732
01:00:47,290 --> 01:00:49,830
"Every action has an equal
and opposite reaction."

733
01:00:51,750 --> 01:00:53,920
In other words, we can call it Karma.

734
01:00:54,290 --> 01:00:57,290
It's like we get the same treatment
we give to others, 

735
01:00:57,830 --> 01:00:59,960
whether it's good or bad.

736
01:01:00,040 --> 01:01:02,290
And that justification comes in Part 2.

737
01:01:03,330 --> 01:01:05,130
Interesting.

738
01:01:05,710 --> 01:01:07,790
I'll be waiting for you.

739
01:01:19,580 --> 01:01:21,670
Sir, you've only seen the reaction.

740
01:01:22,630 --> 01:01:25,170
The action will be revealed
in the second half.

741
01:01:42,540 --> 01:01:48,330
REAL ACTION BEGINS SHORTLY…

742
01:02:06,880 --> 01:02:08,500
- Vinay?
- Yeah.

743
01:02:08,580 --> 01:02:09,960
- Hi.
- Nice to meet you.

744
01:02:10,040 --> 01:02:12,920
I'm David.
I'm in the gold and diamond business.

745
01:02:13,460 --> 01:02:16,170
Why do you live so far from the city?

746
01:02:17,210 --> 01:02:19,460
It's peaceful here.

747
01:02:19,540 --> 01:02:22,500
I feel like I've seen you somewhere.
You look very familiar.

748
01:02:23,880 --> 01:02:25,960
I don't know.

749
01:02:27,460 --> 01:02:29,540
You said you wanted to discuss something?

750
01:02:29,880 --> 01:02:31,920
Oh yeah, I'm just waiting for my partner.

751
01:02:32,000 --> 01:02:34,250
- Meanwhile, can we discuss something?
- Yeah.

752
01:02:34,830 --> 01:02:37,500
Your book. I mean, 
I really enjoyed reading your book.

753
01:02:37,580 --> 01:02:40,330
You said it's based on true events.
Did it really happen?

754
01:02:40,420 --> 01:02:41,750
Are you in touch with them?

755
01:02:41,830 --> 01:02:45,000
Yes. It is a true story, but…

756
01:02:45,330 --> 01:02:48,040
Sorry, I can't reveal my sources.

757
01:02:48,130 --> 01:02:49,290
No, no. It's okay.

758
01:02:49,380 --> 01:02:51,880
At least tell me something about Part 2.

759
01:02:52,880 --> 01:02:55,130
Vasudev, Mercury, Parvathi…

760
01:02:55,210 --> 01:02:57,330
I'm curious how you wrap everything up.

761
01:02:57,420 --> 01:02:59,710
I mean, is Gangadhar still in jail?

762
01:03:00,670 --> 01:03:02,710
Sorry, sir. I can't.

763
01:03:02,790 --> 01:03:05,170
You know, I haven't finished
writing it yet.

764
01:03:05,250 --> 01:03:07,330
So, you'll have to wait.

765
01:03:08,580 --> 01:03:11,080
At least give me a brief idea.

766
01:03:13,750 --> 01:03:15,830
Tell me the bloody Part 2 story!

767
01:03:17,580 --> 01:03:19,670
I'm not going to wait.

768
01:03:22,380 --> 01:03:24,290
Excuse me?

769
01:03:24,380 --> 01:03:28,580
You're not leaving
until you tell me the Part 2 story.

770
01:03:42,540 --> 01:03:44,630
Sit down.

771
01:03:45,880 --> 01:03:47,960
Sit down, I say!

772
01:03:51,790 --> 01:03:55,170
Don't panic. I'm not going to kill you.

773
01:03:56,750 --> 01:03:58,830
I just want to know how the story ends

774
01:03:59,330 --> 01:04:03,500
and exactly what you're going to write, 
down to the last detail.

775
01:04:09,380 --> 01:04:11,460
Relax.

776
01:04:13,330 --> 01:04:17,210
After that, with so many questions
still unanswered…

777
01:04:20,670 --> 01:04:22,750
the only lead Vasudev had was…

778
01:04:30,330 --> 01:04:32,420
Vinay's friend Karthik.

779
01:04:37,290 --> 01:04:39,130
Karthik!

780
01:04:39,210 --> 01:04:40,500
Are you Karthik?

781
01:04:40,580 --> 01:04:42,630
Yes, sir.

782
01:04:42,710 --> 01:04:45,000
We'll speak to that uncle later.
Come with me.

783
01:04:45,670 --> 01:04:47,750
- Did you come from college?
- Yes, sir.

784
01:04:48,250 --> 01:04:50,330
- What's so special today?
- Sir?

785
01:04:50,960 --> 01:04:53,790
You and your friend don't usually
attend college, do you?

786
01:04:53,880 --> 01:04:56,750
- What do you mean by my friend?
- Cut the smart talk.

787
01:05:02,710 --> 01:05:06,880
Sir, you being so polite
really scares me.

788
01:05:07,830 --> 01:05:10,170
Why are you scared? I won't hit you.

789
01:05:11,250 --> 01:05:13,330
But my men will.

790
01:05:14,540 --> 01:05:17,630
I swear on my mother.
I had nothing to do with Vinay.

791
01:05:17,710 --> 01:05:20,670
I just found out from your constable
that he's dead.

792
01:05:23,500 --> 01:05:24,670
I mean it, sir.

793
01:05:24,750 --> 01:05:28,540
You swore on your mother so confidently
because she's dead, right?

794
01:05:29,250 --> 01:05:30,630
Sir?

795
01:05:30,710 --> 01:05:32,460
Wondering how I know?

796
01:05:32,540 --> 01:05:34,250
I'll ask you one question.

797
01:05:34,330 --> 01:05:37,130
Answer honestly, and you can leave.

798
01:05:38,670 --> 01:05:40,880
How many times have you seen me?

799
01:05:41,500 --> 01:05:42,710
First time, sir.

800
01:05:42,790 --> 01:05:44,880
Think carefully.

801
01:05:55,750 --> 01:05:57,830
This is the first time, sir.

802
01:06:02,210 --> 01:06:04,290
What's your connection with Mercury?

803
01:06:07,460 --> 01:06:10,040
I can beat the truth out of you.

804
01:06:11,380 --> 01:06:13,790
You and I both know how Vinay died.

805
01:06:14,290 --> 01:06:19,170
I can easily frame you for his death
and have you locked up for five years.

806
01:06:19,790 --> 01:06:23,880
Even if you've made mistakes, 
I'll let you go if you're honest.

807
01:06:24,330 --> 01:06:26,420
But lie to me even once

808
01:06:26,960 --> 01:06:28,500
and you're finished.

809
01:06:31,880 --> 01:06:33,420
I'll tell you, sir.

810
01:06:33,500 --> 01:06:35,580
I'll tell you everything.

811
01:06:46,080 --> 01:06:48,170
Hey, stop there.

812
01:07:05,960 --> 01:07:06,790
Vinay.

813
01:07:07,880 --> 01:07:10,130
Hey, who are you?
What are you doing here?

814
01:07:12,040 --> 01:07:14,130
Hey!

815
01:07:16,210 --> 01:07:17,420
What are you doing here?

816
01:07:17,500 --> 01:07:18,750
- My bike…
- What?

817
01:07:18,830 --> 01:07:20,920
Jerk.

818
01:07:22,000 --> 01:07:24,210
- Is the bike yours?
- No, please let go of me.

819
01:07:24,290 --> 01:07:26,540
- I'll cut your throat.
- What are you doing?

820
01:07:26,920 --> 01:07:29,580
- Please forgive me. Let me go.
- Get lost!

821
01:07:35,250 --> 01:07:38,130
Vinay knew how to dismantle bike engines, 

822
01:07:38,210 --> 01:07:40,380
and I knew where to sell them safely.

823
01:07:56,750 --> 01:08:00,630
Has your anger waged a war within you?

824
01:08:00,710 --> 01:08:04,670
Has it pushed you relentlessly forward?

825
01:08:04,750 --> 01:08:08,670
Has fate written your life
As a battlefield?

826
01:08:08,750 --> 01:08:12,580
And if it has
Did it ever bring you peace?

827
01:08:12,670 --> 01:08:15,710
The world itself

828
01:08:16,460 --> 01:08:18,670
Has become your target

829
01:08:20,540 --> 01:08:24,630
While your heart has lost its way

830
01:08:24,710 --> 01:08:28,670
Pause for a moment and ask yourself

831
01:08:28,750 --> 01:08:31,540
Where should your gaze truly rest?

832
01:08:39,790 --> 01:08:41,460
Apart from bikes, 
can you do anything else?

833
01:08:41,540 --> 01:08:43,960
I can, but I won't.

834
01:08:48,960 --> 01:08:53,330
Why risk stealing just the engines?
You could've stolen the bikes intact.

835
01:08:53,920 --> 01:08:56,500
How do cops trace a stolen bike?

836
01:08:57,380 --> 01:09:00,330
Using the registration number, 
chassis number, and color.

837
01:09:00,960 --> 01:09:03,040
But what if we steal just the engine?

838
01:09:04,040 --> 01:09:06,830
Before you commit a crime, 
know how to get away with it.

839
01:09:08,330 --> 01:09:10,380
Just bike engines, or anything else?

840
01:09:10,460 --> 01:09:13,670
We also placed bets
to double our earnings.

841
01:09:37,880 --> 01:09:39,750
Fast in the lane
Never slow, no change

842
01:09:39,830 --> 01:09:41,710
Breaking the limits
My flow unchanged

843
01:09:41,830 --> 01:09:43,790
Came with the flame
Put the game to the shame

844
01:09:43,880 --> 01:09:45,790
Rewire my deliver
I'm insane with the aim

845
01:09:45,880 --> 01:09:47,830
Wraiths can't catch me
Speed of the sound

846
01:09:47,920 --> 01:09:49,830
Ground gonna shatter
When my work gets bound

847
01:09:49,920 --> 01:09:51,670
Crown is my goal
Gotta take it now

848
01:09:51,750 --> 01:09:53,830
You blink and you'll mistake this round

849
01:10:10,210 --> 01:10:13,920
Why this hurry

850
01:10:14,000 --> 01:10:17,380
To win at all costs?

851
01:10:18,210 --> 01:10:22,130
Without competition
Victory has no meaning

852
01:10:22,210 --> 01:10:25,880
Without a worthy game
The contest isn't right

853
01:10:25,960 --> 01:10:29,920
If you listen to wisdom

854
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:34,130
Society will stand beside you

855
01:10:34,210 --> 01:10:38,290
But if stubborn pride
Becomes your path

856
01:10:38,380 --> 01:10:41,830
You'll walk alone

857
01:10:41,920 --> 01:10:45,830
Even fortune's favor ends in strife

858
01:10:45,920 --> 01:10:49,250
And sinks into an endless abyss

859
01:10:49,330 --> 01:10:50,290
Back off!

860
01:10:50,380 --> 01:10:53,580
This may sound too philosophical

861
01:10:53,920 --> 01:10:57,080
It'd be a surprise if you listened to it

862
01:10:57,670 --> 01:11:00,210
The world itself

863
01:11:01,580 --> 01:11:03,830
Has become your target

864
01:11:05,630 --> 01:11:09,290
While your heart has lost its way

865
01:11:09,670 --> 01:11:13,790
Where should your gaze truly rest?

866
01:11:13,880 --> 01:11:16,750
The noose of death may already be waiting

867
01:11:35,630 --> 01:11:38,580
One day, Vinay called me
and came over to my place.

868
01:11:40,710 --> 01:11:43,830
Mom, tell me. How much do we need
to solve all our problems?

869
01:11:43,920 --> 01:11:46,000
What's your ambition in life?

870
01:11:48,710 --> 01:11:51,330
Well, Mr. Robin Hood, 
you said you wanted to talk.

871
01:11:52,580 --> 01:11:54,670
So, you've already been drinking.

872
01:11:55,290 --> 01:11:57,920
I see. What's the issue now?

873
01:12:03,130 --> 01:12:05,210
What's your ambition in life?

874
01:12:10,540 --> 01:12:13,710
Mine won't sound very nice. You go first.

875
01:12:18,330 --> 01:12:21,080
Yours is the same, isn't it?

876
01:12:22,250 --> 01:12:24,750
No, man. I want to fill a bag with cash, 

877
01:12:25,250 --> 01:12:28,500
put it in front of my parents, 
look my father in the eye, 

878
01:12:29,040 --> 01:12:33,380
and ask him for a full list of our debts
so I can pay them all off in a single day.

879
01:12:33,460 --> 01:12:35,540
Then I want to look at my mom…

880
01:12:37,880 --> 01:12:41,040
and tell her that our problems are over

881
01:12:42,080 --> 01:12:44,170
and our lives will change.

882
01:12:46,830 --> 01:12:50,040
It may hurt my dad's ego, 
but he'll finally be happy.

883
01:12:51,630 --> 01:12:53,460
And my mom will be proud of me.

884
01:12:53,540 --> 01:12:57,290
To make that happen, we have to stop
these petty thefts and betting.

885
01:12:57,380 --> 01:12:59,540
We need to take a big risk.

886
01:12:59,630 --> 01:13:02,790
A scam, a heist, money laundering, 
or something big.

887
01:13:04,880 --> 01:13:06,960
I understand how you feel.

888
01:13:07,920 --> 01:13:10,000
But do we really need that right now?

889
01:13:13,710 --> 01:13:17,130
Do you remember the robbery
at our jewelry shop three years ago?

890
01:13:18,790 --> 01:13:21,540
That's when my father started drinking.

891
01:13:22,960 --> 01:13:25,040
He hasn't stopped since.

892
01:13:25,750 --> 01:13:29,920
My mom began working overtime
and night shifts, 

893
01:13:30,500 --> 01:13:32,210
and she's still at it.

894
01:13:32,290 --> 01:13:35,130
Someone robbed us, 
and this is where we ended up.

895
01:13:35,750 --> 01:13:38,710
Whoever did it
must've had their life sorted, right?

896
01:13:40,330 --> 01:13:42,790
Forget that they robbed someone
to make it happen.

897
01:13:44,000 --> 01:13:48,290
They have no worries about the future
and no regrets about the past.

898
01:13:49,130 --> 01:13:51,380
They're respected, 
and they live comfortably.

899
01:13:53,000 --> 01:13:55,080
I want that life too.

900
01:13:55,540 --> 01:13:57,790
I'm done with these small-time jobs.

901
01:13:58,540 --> 01:14:00,670
One big move, and we'll be set for life.

902
01:14:00,750 --> 01:14:02,830
Do you really think it's worth the risk?

903
01:14:04,710 --> 01:14:06,790
The risk isn't in what we do, Karthik.

904
01:14:07,250 --> 01:14:09,460
It's in how we do it.

905
01:14:12,710 --> 01:14:15,540
We stopped the petty theft
for a while, sir.

906
01:14:16,080 --> 01:14:18,750
As Vinay wanted, we were waiting
for an opportunity

907
01:14:19,290 --> 01:14:20,880
that could change our lives.

908
01:14:20,960 --> 01:14:23,380
Then we got an offer through our contacts.

909
01:14:24,420 --> 01:14:26,750
It's not the big job we hoped for.

910
01:14:27,130 --> 01:14:29,580
Just a small task worth 20, 000 rupees.

911
01:14:33,790 --> 01:14:37,080
Just pick someone up and drop them
somewhere tomorrow night.

912
01:14:37,170 --> 01:14:38,460
They'll pay us 20, 000 rupees.

913
01:14:38,540 --> 01:14:40,960
I've arranged the car. The deal's fixed.

914
01:14:42,250 --> 01:14:43,830
Did Khalid set this up?

915
01:14:43,920 --> 01:14:47,130
Not just me. Even the person
who passed the deal on to me

916
01:14:47,210 --> 01:14:49,210
doesn't know who's behind it.

917
01:14:49,290 --> 01:14:52,580
So stop worrying and just do the job.
It'll work out for you.

918
01:14:52,670 --> 01:14:54,920
Be ready with the car tomorrow at 10 p.m.

919
01:14:55,000 --> 01:14:57,290
You'll get the drop-off location
by message

920
01:14:57,380 --> 01:14:59,500
and the instructions once you arrive.

921
01:15:00,380 --> 01:15:03,580
Don't you see what this means?
They're planning something big.

922
01:15:04,580 --> 01:15:06,670
And we're getting a paltry 20, 000 rupees.

923
01:15:07,250 --> 01:15:09,330
Fine, what do you think it is?

924
01:15:11,460 --> 01:15:12,960
It could be a bank robbery, 

925
01:15:13,040 --> 01:15:17,420
a jewelry heist, a drug deal, 
smuggling, hawala.

926
01:15:17,790 --> 01:15:19,540
Anything like that.

927
01:15:19,630 --> 01:15:21,250
Once they're done with the job, 

928
01:15:21,330 --> 01:15:24,830
they'll travel in strangers' vehicles
to avoid getting caught.

929
01:15:24,920 --> 01:15:26,830
So they'll use strangers like us.

930
01:15:26,920 --> 01:15:29,830
You must be watching too many
Quentin Tarantino films.

931
01:15:29,920 --> 01:15:32,000
Wait. Hear me out.

932
01:15:32,580 --> 01:15:34,920
They haven't given us
the pick-up location yet.

933
01:15:35,040 --> 01:15:37,130
It'd be risky for them to tell us now.

934
01:15:37,380 --> 01:15:42,210
We pick up, drop off, take the money, 
grab a few beers, and sleep it off.

935
01:15:43,580 --> 01:15:47,420
Mess this up, and we won't get work again.

936
01:15:52,670 --> 01:15:54,750
So you really think nothing's going on?

937
01:15:55,960 --> 01:15:59,420
You suspect something too.
You're just scared to take the risk.

938
01:15:59,500 --> 01:16:02,630
And you don't feel the urgency either.
Fine, stay out of it.

939
01:16:03,210 --> 01:16:05,290
If I pull it off, you get no share.

940
01:16:06,000 --> 01:16:08,330
And after this, I'm done with all of it.

941
01:16:08,670 --> 01:16:11,330
This will be our last job together.

942
01:16:20,540 --> 01:16:22,630
Alright then, what's the plan?

943
01:16:29,210 --> 01:16:31,290
We need to take a big risk.

944
01:17:17,290 --> 01:17:19,040
Going to a movie. I'll eat outside.

945
01:17:19,130 --> 01:17:21,210
Did you take your keys?

946
01:17:23,830 --> 01:17:25,920
He remembers this well.

947
01:17:34,460 --> 01:17:36,670
- Wear this T-shirt.
- Why?

948
01:17:36,750 --> 01:17:39,710
- Are we playing cricket?
- Just do as I say.

949
01:17:40,420 --> 01:17:42,210
When we meet someone new, 

950
01:17:42,290 --> 01:17:46,960
changing our look makes it harder for them
to recognize us later.

951
01:17:47,420 --> 01:17:49,420
- It's a psychological theory.
- Hey…

952
01:17:49,500 --> 01:17:50,710
Stop it, please.

953
01:17:50,790 --> 01:17:52,920
I think you just watched a Hollywood film.

954
01:17:53,000 --> 01:17:55,460
- You want me to wear it? I'll wear it.
- Go ahead.

955
01:18:05,960 --> 01:18:08,170
Good. Listen carefully. Plan A.

956
01:18:08,670 --> 01:18:10,420
We make him sit here, 

957
01:18:10,500 --> 01:18:14,500
spray chloroform on this hanky, 
and hold it to his nose for 30 seconds.

958
01:18:14,580 --> 01:18:17,500
He'll be knocked out, and we take control.

959
01:18:17,580 --> 01:18:20,630
What if he's stronger than us?

960
01:18:20,710 --> 01:18:23,580
Then Plan B.
The moment you honk, 

961
01:18:23,880 --> 01:18:26,830
I'll spray chloroform throughout
the car from the back seat.

962
01:18:26,920 --> 01:18:30,330
He'll be unconscious in a minute, 
and we'll be in control again.

963
01:18:30,790 --> 01:18:33,040
But we'll inhale it too, won't we?

964
01:18:34,420 --> 01:18:36,330
How long can you hold your breath?

965
01:18:36,420 --> 01:18:38,540
- Actually, I haven't tried it before.
- Hey!

966
01:18:39,000 --> 01:18:41,130
If we try, we can manage up to a minute.

967
01:18:41,210 --> 01:18:43,380
What if he rolls down the window?

968
01:18:45,210 --> 01:18:48,710
Then Plan C. There's no way it can fail.

969
01:18:51,460 --> 01:18:53,750
We point the gun at him
at point-blank range

970
01:18:53,830 --> 01:18:55,540
and he'll be terrified.

971
01:18:55,630 --> 01:18:57,710
Where did you get that gun?

972
01:18:57,920 --> 01:18:59,710
My dad used to have an antique shop.

973
01:18:59,790 --> 01:19:02,710
Even though it was illegal, 
my dad used to sell these guns.

974
01:19:02,920 --> 01:19:04,880
- I got it from there.
- Does it work?

975
01:19:04,960 --> 01:19:07,040
Idiot, there's a bullet in it.

976
01:19:07,540 --> 01:19:09,830
What? Are you planning to kill him?

977
01:19:11,630 --> 01:19:14,750
They say every grain of rice reaches
the person destined to eat it.

978
01:19:14,830 --> 01:19:19,330
If that's true, then so does every bullet.

979
01:19:21,380 --> 01:19:23,460
Let's see who it's meant to hit.

980
01:19:25,290 --> 01:19:27,380
Hey, we've got a message.

981
01:19:31,540 --> 01:19:35,790
"Sharp at 1:30 a.m., Lingampally, 
Old Steel Factory, Back Street Lane."

982
01:19:38,380 --> 01:19:39,830
Karthik.

983
01:19:39,920 --> 01:19:42,130
Keep this in mind.

984
01:19:42,210 --> 01:19:44,330
Don't be scared. Be confident.

985
01:19:46,170 --> 01:19:47,580
Come on.

986
01:19:58,830 --> 01:20:00,960
- Hey, turn right.
- Not here, man.

987
01:20:01,040 --> 01:20:03,130
I know the way. Turn right.

988
01:20:08,830 --> 01:20:11,540
- Pull over on the left.
- What's there?

989
01:20:18,000 --> 01:20:20,580
I guess this isn't the place.
It's the street behind.

990
01:20:21,130 --> 01:20:22,000
I know.

991
01:20:22,080 --> 01:20:25,460
They asked us to come at exactly 1:30 a.m.
We still have 20 minutes.

992
01:20:25,540 --> 01:20:27,710
We shouldn't arrive too early or too late.

993
01:20:27,790 --> 01:20:30,670
- Shall we have a puff?
- We're not here to puff or piss.

994
01:20:31,330 --> 01:20:33,710
- We're here to observe them.
- Fine, come on.

995
01:20:36,500 --> 01:20:38,420
Hey, watch it! Keep it down!

996
01:20:38,500 --> 01:20:39,920
Okay, okay.

997
01:21:09,830 --> 01:21:11,630
Hey!

998
01:21:11,710 --> 01:21:13,790
I'll deal with you later.

999
01:21:17,670 --> 01:21:20,130
You said there'd be just one guy.
There are many.

1000
01:21:20,210 --> 01:21:23,000
- How would I know? They told me nothing.
- What the heck!

1001
01:21:49,210 --> 01:21:51,500
There are only two ways to rise, George.

1002
01:21:52,630 --> 01:21:55,920
One is by using your brain.

1003
01:21:57,000 --> 01:22:00,330
The other is by using a gun.

1004
01:22:01,580 --> 01:22:04,040
I reached this position using both.

1005
01:22:04,500 --> 01:22:07,380
That's what you call brilliance.

1006
01:22:08,420 --> 01:22:12,630
And now, if you want to crush me
and surpass me, 

1007
01:22:13,420 --> 01:22:15,500
what will you use?

1008
01:22:20,960 --> 01:22:23,130
We were so happy, weren't we, George?

1009
01:22:23,210 --> 01:22:26,040
Murders, smuggling, robberies, 
and whatnot.

1010
01:22:27,460 --> 01:22:30,080
What will you gain
by turning me in to the police?

1011
01:22:30,920 --> 01:22:34,290
Oh! You want a bigger cut?

1012
01:22:34,670 --> 01:22:37,420
One shouldn't aim
above one's station, George.

1013
01:22:37,500 --> 01:22:39,750
That's where problems begin.

1014
01:22:43,250 --> 01:22:45,380
Oh, dear. Oh boy.

1015
01:22:45,460 --> 01:22:47,540
Oh boy.

1016
01:22:48,460 --> 01:22:50,540
Does it hurt?

1017
01:22:50,920 --> 01:22:53,420
That's okay. Give me two minutes.

1018
01:22:53,830 --> 01:22:55,330
I'll kill you.

1019
01:22:55,420 --> 01:22:57,500
He's a psycho.

1020
01:23:02,880 --> 01:23:05,630
- No, no!
- Rest in peace, George.

1021
01:23:20,880 --> 01:23:23,580
This is your cut. Take it.

1022
01:23:31,000 --> 01:23:33,080
Vinay, let's go.

1023
01:23:36,250 --> 01:23:38,670
It's not too late to change our minds.

1024
01:23:39,290 --> 01:23:41,830
Let's do our job and leave.
Don't act smart.

1025
01:23:42,790 --> 01:23:46,710
We weren't supposed to get into this.
But now that we have, we can't back out.

1026
01:23:48,540 --> 01:23:50,630
We've got the drop location.

1027
01:24:18,880 --> 01:24:20,540
You were told to come alone.

1028
01:24:20,630 --> 01:24:23,330
Sir… he's my friend…

1029
01:24:23,420 --> 01:24:26,080
It's okay, open the trunk.

1030
01:24:38,750 --> 01:24:40,830
It's okay. I'll take care.

1031
01:24:55,630 --> 01:24:57,710
Plan A. Plan B.

1032
01:24:58,170 --> 01:25:01,250
Plan C. There's no way it can fail.

1033
01:25:07,000 --> 01:25:07,960
Hey.

1034
01:25:08,040 --> 01:25:08,880
Sir?

1035
01:25:08,960 --> 01:25:11,040
Sit in the front seat.

1036
01:25:16,630 --> 01:25:18,710
One second.

1037
01:25:22,130 --> 01:25:24,210
You know how to drive, right?

1038
01:25:24,750 --> 01:25:26,830
- Yes, sir.
- Switch seats.

1039
01:25:33,420 --> 01:25:35,500
Don't we have Plan D?

1040
01:26:12,710 --> 01:26:14,960
How much do we need
to solve all our problems?

1041
01:26:15,540 --> 01:26:19,540
We weren't supposed to get into this.
But now that we have, we can't back out.

1042
01:26:20,420 --> 01:26:24,630
The risk isn't in what we do, Karthik.
It's in how we do it.

1043
01:26:29,960 --> 01:26:32,290
Hey!

1044
01:26:35,170 --> 01:26:37,250
Watch out!

1045
01:28:00,830 --> 01:28:01,670
Shravya…

1046
01:28:02,210 --> 01:28:04,290
Dude, we just hit someone!

1047
01:28:06,790 --> 01:28:08,880
Diamonds, man.

1048
01:28:10,080 --> 01:28:12,210
They're real diamonds.

1049
01:28:15,330 --> 01:28:17,420
What do we do with him? Dump him here?

1050
01:28:19,420 --> 01:28:22,130
Not here. Let's dump him somewhere else.

1051
01:28:23,380 --> 01:28:25,460
Hey, what about the person we hit?

1052
01:28:29,500 --> 01:28:31,670
Hey, think carefully.

1053
01:28:31,750 --> 01:28:33,830
We need to escape before he wakes up.

1054
01:28:34,420 --> 01:28:37,420
Dude, I want to get out and save her too.

1055
01:28:40,130 --> 01:28:42,210
But I can't risk it.

1056
01:28:46,380 --> 01:28:49,960
We can't stay here any longer.
The accident victim or the diamonds?

1057
01:29:28,500 --> 01:29:30,710
Hey, hey!

1058
01:29:30,790 --> 01:29:33,710
This wasn't a petty robbery.

1059
01:29:34,330 --> 01:29:36,750
There'll be a serious investigation
for a while.

1060
01:29:37,290 --> 01:29:39,380
Let's lie low for a month, okay?

1061
01:29:42,920 --> 01:29:46,290
Listen, it's risky to keep
the diamonds at your place.

1062
01:29:46,460 --> 01:29:48,250
I'll keep them safe at my house.

1063
01:29:48,500 --> 01:29:50,580
Are you okay with it? Yes, you are.

1064
01:29:51,460 --> 01:29:53,880
- Who said I'm okay?
- Listen to me, man.

1065
01:29:54,830 --> 01:29:57,130
Don't come out for a week.

1066
01:29:57,210 --> 01:30:00,080
It's too risky.
If possible, go back to your village.

1067
01:30:00,630 --> 01:30:02,710
Khalid doesn't know my address.

1068
01:30:03,290 --> 01:30:05,330
But I think he knows your address.

1069
01:30:05,420 --> 01:30:07,250
No, he doesn't.

1070
01:30:07,330 --> 01:30:09,540
I'll switch off my phone if needed.

1071
01:30:09,630 --> 01:30:11,710
We did it, man!

1072
01:30:20,080 --> 01:30:22,290
- What's the matter?
- The corpse in the trunk.

1073
01:30:25,830 --> 01:30:27,920
What do we do?

1074
01:30:56,880 --> 01:30:58,420
There's cash in this bag.

1075
01:30:58,500 --> 01:31:00,960
Let's clear all our debts today.

1076
01:31:03,710 --> 01:31:06,380
Mom, you don't need to work
night shifts anymore.

1077
01:31:07,210 --> 01:31:10,250
You want the three of us
to enjoy a meal together, right?

1078
01:31:10,330 --> 01:31:12,420
It'll happen today.

1079
01:31:16,130 --> 01:31:18,210
Hello? Hello?

1080
01:31:30,380 --> 01:31:31,380
Hello?

1081
01:31:31,460 --> 01:31:32,710
Hey, it's me.

1082
01:31:32,790 --> 01:31:35,330
Tell me, why did you call the landline?

1083
01:31:35,420 --> 01:31:37,500
You switched off your phone.

1084
01:31:38,630 --> 01:31:40,250
Yeah, tell me.

1085
01:31:40,330 --> 01:31:42,250
Bring those diamonds to my place.

1086
01:31:42,330 --> 01:31:43,710
I told you last night.

1087
01:31:43,790 --> 01:31:45,880
I didn't agree to what you said.

1088
01:31:46,830 --> 01:31:48,540
I think I've found a buyer.

1089
01:31:48,630 --> 01:31:50,960
Bring the diamonds, and let's make a deal.

1090
01:31:54,290 --> 01:31:55,830
Hey, I'll call you later.

1091
01:31:56,210 --> 01:31:58,000
Hello? Hello?

1092
01:32:03,040 --> 01:32:05,130
Where are the diamonds?

1093
01:32:33,210 --> 01:32:34,880
What did you lose this time?

1094
01:32:34,960 --> 01:32:36,540
I'm talking to you.

1095
01:32:36,630 --> 01:32:39,330
I'll search for it too, 
if you tell me what it is.

1096
01:32:40,250 --> 01:32:43,330
You even forgot what you're looking for?
Where did you put it?

1097
01:32:43,420 --> 01:32:45,500
If I knew, I'd look there myself!

1098
01:32:47,250 --> 01:32:50,880
Hey, don't you know I forget everything
when I drink?

1099
01:32:51,330 --> 01:32:54,750
I'm sure the diamonds are in my house.
Just give me a week.

1100
01:32:54,830 --> 01:32:57,000
- After that--
- I know what to do after that.

1101
01:33:00,750 --> 01:33:04,170
Not a week. I'll give you four days.

1102
01:33:04,250 --> 01:33:06,330
That's it.

1103
01:33:06,790 --> 01:33:08,880
Just four more days.

1104
01:33:15,040 --> 01:33:17,130
Shit!

1105
01:33:17,710 --> 01:33:19,790
Plan A.

1106
01:33:20,210 --> 01:33:22,040
Plan B.

1107
01:33:22,130 --> 01:33:24,210
Plan C.

1108
01:33:25,290 --> 01:33:27,250
Plan A.

1109
01:33:27,330 --> 01:33:29,380
Plan B.

1110
01:33:29,460 --> 01:33:31,580
Plan C.

1111
01:33:31,670 --> 01:33:32,920
Not Plan C.

1112
01:33:33,000 --> 01:33:34,460
Plan C.

1113
01:33:37,460 --> 01:33:39,540
Plan C.

1114
01:33:43,500 --> 01:33:45,580
Plan C.

1115
01:33:50,000 --> 01:33:51,580
Karthik.

1116
01:33:52,040 --> 01:33:54,170
Keep this in mind.

1117
01:33:54,250 --> 01:33:56,540
Don't be scared. Be confident.

1118
01:33:57,080 --> 01:33:58,540
Come on.

1119
01:34:13,920 --> 01:34:17,750
We weren't supposed to get into this.
But now that we have, we can't back out.

1120
01:34:18,080 --> 01:34:20,290
The risk isn't in what we do, Karthik.

1121
01:34:20,380 --> 01:34:22,460
It's in how we do it.

1122
01:34:24,580 --> 01:34:26,710
It's in how we do it.

1123
01:34:44,420 --> 01:34:46,500
It's in how we do it.

1124
01:34:48,750 --> 01:34:50,500
It's in how we do it.

1125
01:34:50,580 --> 01:34:54,710
Has your anger waged a war within you?

1126
01:34:54,790 --> 01:34:58,790
Has it pushed you relentlessly forward?

1127
01:34:58,880 --> 01:35:02,790
Has fate written your life
As a battlefield?

1128
01:35:02,880 --> 01:35:06,880
And if it has
Did it ever bring you peace?

1129
01:35:16,130 --> 01:35:17,630
What else, Vinay?

1130
01:35:18,080 --> 01:35:20,830
I've searched the entire house.
I'm not trying to cheat you.

1131
01:35:20,920 --> 01:35:23,250
I need those diamonds
just as much as you do.

1132
01:35:26,080 --> 01:35:28,540
Besides, I took more risks than you did.

1133
01:35:33,210 --> 01:35:35,290
- Fine, leave it, then.
- Hey.

1134
01:35:38,250 --> 01:35:40,330
- So, what now?
- What else can we do?

1135
01:35:41,000 --> 01:35:43,420
I'm not in the right frame of mind.
I'm leaving.

1136
01:35:50,670 --> 01:35:52,830
Shall we have a drink?
I'm really irritated.

1137
01:35:53,750 --> 01:35:55,250
It'll help.

1138
01:35:55,330 --> 01:35:56,580
Now?

1139
01:36:02,380 --> 01:36:03,420
Is your dad home?

1140
01:36:03,500 --> 01:36:04,750
I don't think so.

1141
01:36:14,210 --> 01:36:17,830
- Why have you made it so strong?
- It tastes like this after a long break.

1142
01:36:17,920 --> 01:36:20,420
I still think if we search your house
again, 

1143
01:36:20,540 --> 01:36:21,750
we'll find the diamonds.

1144
01:36:21,830 --> 01:36:22,880
Sit down!

1145
01:36:23,500 --> 01:36:25,960
I searched every inch
except the toilet tanks.

1146
01:36:26,170 --> 01:36:29,250
Let's forget about them.
We'll come across them eventually.

1147
01:36:36,250 --> 01:36:39,250
- Do we really need this now?
- It works better than the drink.

1148
01:36:57,000 --> 01:36:58,500
How's that?

1149
01:37:02,420 --> 01:37:04,080
What are you laughing at?

1150
01:37:11,630 --> 01:37:13,380
Where did you put the diamonds?

1151
01:37:14,580 --> 01:37:16,670
Mate, I told you I don't remember.

1152
01:37:16,750 --> 01:37:18,250
Just listen to me.

1153
01:37:18,330 --> 01:37:20,380
I think someone's following us.

1154
01:37:20,460 --> 01:37:23,630
When I ride the bike, it feels like
someone's sitting behind me.

1155
01:37:23,750 --> 01:37:27,460
Even now, I feel like someone's
sitting on that sofa, watching us.

1156
01:37:28,540 --> 01:37:32,080
It's like I'm being
psychologically haunted.

1157
01:37:33,250 --> 01:37:36,790
Oh, come on. Here he goes again
with another story.

1158
01:37:36,920 --> 01:37:38,040
What?

1159
01:37:40,580 --> 01:37:42,670
I think I know what's going on.

1160
01:37:43,380 --> 01:37:46,580
You killed someone in that accident.

1161
01:37:47,460 --> 01:37:48,580
Remember?

1162
01:37:48,670 --> 01:37:49,920
Hey, dude, 

1163
01:37:50,040 --> 01:37:55,000
do you think that person's ghost
is following you?

1164
01:38:27,000 --> 01:38:28,040
I'll get some water.

1165
01:38:28,130 --> 01:38:33,000
Oh, my darling, 
I'll shower you with riches

1166
01:38:34,330 --> 01:38:35,540
There's no water.

1167
01:38:37,750 --> 01:38:39,540
Alright, this ice will do.

1168
01:38:39,880 --> 01:38:41,960
I want it all, my dear

1169
01:38:42,290 --> 01:38:44,920
Let's stay up tonight, Karthik

1170
01:38:45,080 --> 01:38:46,250
One more.

1171
01:38:48,290 --> 01:38:49,670
Another clink.

1172
01:38:50,380 --> 01:38:52,000
Hey, Vinay!

1173
01:38:54,540 --> 01:38:56,670
Where are the diamonds?

1174
01:38:56,750 --> 01:39:00,080
Karthik, have you lost it?

1175
01:39:01,420 --> 01:39:04,670
I told you to forget about them.

1176
01:39:04,750 --> 01:39:08,960
I watched a Korean movie
when my parents weren't home.

1177
01:39:09,830 --> 01:39:12,170
Red Flower With Yellow Petals.

1178
01:39:12,460 --> 01:39:15,500
Wow! The romance was brilliant.

1179
01:39:15,630 --> 01:39:16,710
Oh, stop it!

1180
01:39:16,790 --> 01:39:19,460
You're clearly not drunk. Listen to me.

1181
01:39:20,000 --> 01:39:24,920
If you really couldn't find them, 
I think your dad took the diamonds.

1182
01:39:27,460 --> 01:39:29,330
What are you implying?

1183
01:39:29,420 --> 01:39:31,420
That my dad and I are in this together?

1184
01:39:31,500 --> 01:39:34,380
That's not what I meant.
Your dad needs money.

1185
01:39:34,460 --> 01:39:37,380
He just sits at home and gets an earful.
So he--

1186
01:39:37,460 --> 01:39:39,130
What are you getting at?

1187
01:39:39,790 --> 01:39:41,540
- Forget it.
- Forget it.

1188
01:39:44,460 --> 01:39:46,750
Just give me my share. I'll just leave.

1189
01:39:46,830 --> 01:39:48,960
We'll see once we find the diamonds.

1190
01:39:49,040 --> 01:39:51,130
Even if we find them, 

1191
01:39:51,330 --> 01:39:56,920
I get 75 percent and you get 25 percent
of their total worth.

1192
01:39:57,080 --> 01:39:58,040
Oh, really?

1193
01:39:58,130 --> 01:40:00,830
I'm the one who dismantled
the bike engines.

1194
01:40:00,920 --> 01:40:02,420
Who sold them? Your dad?

1195
01:40:02,500 --> 01:40:04,580
If not you, someone else would have.

1196
01:40:04,920 --> 01:40:07,000
I planned everything.

1197
01:40:07,790 --> 01:40:09,790
I executed it.

1198
01:40:10,000 --> 01:40:11,250
I took the risks.

1199
01:40:11,330 --> 01:40:12,540
What exactly did you do?

1200
01:40:12,710 --> 01:40:15,880
You sat in the car pissing yourself.
25 percent is generous.

1201
01:40:15,960 --> 01:40:18,040
Could you have done it alone?

1202
01:40:23,710 --> 01:40:25,790
Who brought us the deal
in the first place?

1203
01:40:26,920 --> 01:40:30,750
A waiter gets a tip, not the bill.

1204
01:40:35,080 --> 01:40:36,670
Take your share.

1205
01:40:37,170 --> 01:40:38,790
Share my foot!

1206
01:41:16,580 --> 01:41:19,500
I'll keep them safe at my house.

1207
01:41:21,080 --> 01:41:23,170
I need to hide them properly.

1208
01:41:24,000 --> 01:41:26,080
If I leave them here, Mom will notice.

1209
01:41:39,630 --> 01:41:41,170
Alright, this ice will do.

1210
01:42:07,380 --> 01:42:09,750
Karthik, let's go smoke on the balcony.

1211
01:42:09,880 --> 01:42:12,040
Hey! Are you mad?

1212
01:42:12,500 --> 01:42:13,960
You're completely drunk.

1213
01:42:14,330 --> 01:42:16,040
I'll drink some more. So what?

1214
01:42:16,130 --> 01:42:18,290
- Come on, let's have a cigarette.
- Hey!

1215
01:45:00,380 --> 01:45:03,630
Maybe this bullet is meant for you.
Want to find out?

1216
01:45:21,000 --> 01:45:23,420
Two days later, I called him again.

1217
01:45:28,080 --> 01:45:28,960
Hello?

1218
01:45:29,130 --> 01:45:31,000
Ma'am, it's Karthik. Is Vinay there?

1219
01:45:33,250 --> 01:45:34,460
- Vinay?
- Yes.

1220
01:45:34,540 --> 01:45:35,830
Karthik is on the phone.

1221
01:45:36,040 --> 01:45:37,250
Coming, Mom.

1222
01:45:44,380 --> 01:45:45,500
Yes, tell me.

1223
01:45:45,580 --> 01:45:47,670
"Speeding claims a life."

1224
01:45:48,000 --> 01:45:50,710
"A five-year-old is left orphaned."

1225
01:45:51,250 --> 01:45:53,580
"Police are searching for the culprit."

1226
01:45:55,750 --> 01:45:57,250
Listen, DiCaprio.

1227
01:45:57,330 --> 01:45:59,330
It takes me 15 minutes to walk, 

1228
01:45:59,420 --> 01:46:03,040
or just two minutes by bike, 
to get to the police station.

1229
01:46:03,960 --> 01:46:05,420
Should I go there?

1230
01:46:13,250 --> 01:46:15,580
Oh, my darling

1231
01:46:16,750 --> 01:46:19,960
I'll shower you with riches

1232
01:46:20,790 --> 01:46:23,420
I want it, my dear

1233
01:46:24,170 --> 01:46:27,670
Give me my share, love

1234
01:46:31,670 --> 01:46:34,330
Eucalyptus sodium crystals.

1235
01:46:35,250 --> 01:46:36,580
It's a new chemical.

1236
01:46:38,250 --> 01:46:40,880
They're mixing it into rum
to heighten the effect.

1237
01:46:42,630 --> 01:46:46,040
People go mad after drinking it, 
like we did last time.

1238
01:46:50,210 --> 01:46:52,670
I think our bottle was spiked too.

1239
01:46:55,040 --> 01:46:57,130
Don't be ridiculous.

1240
01:46:58,750 --> 01:47:01,710
I drank the same thing and I'm fine.

1241
01:47:02,250 --> 01:47:03,920
Eucalyptus, my foot.

1242
01:47:04,130 --> 01:47:05,420
What rubbish!

1243
01:47:13,920 --> 01:47:16,330
There are two reasons you came to me.

1244
01:47:16,750 --> 01:47:19,250
One is that accident, and the other is…

1245
01:47:20,460 --> 01:47:23,250
You're worried I'll tell our deal guy
where you live.

1246
01:47:24,000 --> 01:47:27,710
Before these two things happen, 
give me my cut and I'll leave.

1247
01:47:28,460 --> 01:47:31,080
Not two. There are three reasons.

1248
01:47:31,330 --> 01:47:32,750
The third reason is…

1249
01:47:33,080 --> 01:47:35,880
I've forgotten where I kept
those diamonds again.

1250
01:47:38,710 --> 01:47:39,880
Oh God!

1251
01:47:40,080 --> 01:47:42,790
Hey! I don't care, 
and I don't believe you.

1252
01:47:43,130 --> 01:47:45,460
Don't you know me?
You have a bad memory.

1253
01:47:45,540 --> 01:47:48,580
I told you, I forget where I put things
when I'm drunk.

1254
01:47:48,670 --> 01:47:50,750
I don't care. I want my share now.

1255
01:47:51,210 --> 01:47:53,960
I'm not trying to cheat you.
See for yourself.

1256
01:47:54,500 --> 01:47:56,750
- I've kept my phone on.
- Shove it in your bum.

1257
01:47:56,830 --> 01:47:58,920
I don't care. Give me my share.

1258
01:48:03,830 --> 01:48:04,880
Hey, shh.

1259
01:48:20,080 --> 01:48:21,330
Tissue, please.

1260
01:48:24,960 --> 01:48:26,040
Thank you.

1261
01:48:31,130 --> 01:48:32,580
Did he recognize us?

1262
01:48:48,920 --> 01:48:51,790
Sir, the exit is that way, not this way.

1263
01:48:52,250 --> 01:48:53,830
Aren't you roaming outside?

1264
01:48:53,920 --> 01:48:55,460
Oh my!

1265
01:48:55,540 --> 01:48:58,250
Is that you? We met before, didn't we?

1266
01:48:59,580 --> 01:49:00,540
Hey…

1267
01:49:02,540 --> 01:49:05,710
We gave someone a lift last week.
It's him.

1268
01:49:06,420 --> 01:49:09,330
I heard everything.
I'll get straight to the point.

1269
01:49:10,210 --> 01:49:11,580
Where are the diamonds?

1270
01:49:11,920 --> 01:49:14,210
He's asking for the diamonds.
Give them to him.

1271
01:49:14,670 --> 01:49:18,750
By the way, if you've heard everything, 
why are you asking for the diamonds?

1272
01:49:19,920 --> 01:49:22,750
He just said he forgot everything and--

1273
01:49:44,040 --> 01:49:45,880
Sit down right where you are.

1274
01:49:46,580 --> 01:49:48,540
- Sir--
